* [`ag.cluster_picture`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Background/Algebraic-geometry/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_ag___cluster_picture_FLQQ_--statement) — Cluster picture. Declarations (LeanBridge): `Polynomial.IsPadicCluster`, `Polynomial.padicClusterSize`, `Polynomial.padicClusterValDepth`, `Polynomial.padicClusterRelValDepth`, `Polynomial.IsPadicCluster.subset_or_subset_or_disjoint`, `Polynomial.IsPadicCluster.isPadicCluster_padicClusterParent`. Note: Both gaps are closed. The tree structure: two clusters are nested or disjoint (subset\_or\_subset\_or\_disjoint, from Mathlib's ultrametric closedBall\_subset\_trichotomy), so for a cluster other than the top one the strictly larger clusters form a nonempty finite chain and padicClusterParent, their intersection, is a cluster strictly containing it (isPadicCluster\_padicClusterParent, ssubset\_padicClusterParent) and contained in every such cluster (padicClusterParent\_subset): the smallest other cluster containing it. The depth: in an ultrametric space the diameter of a nonempty bounded set is the least radius of a closed disc containing it (IsUltrametricDist.isLeast\_diam), and the new extended-real depth padicClusterValDepth is -log\_p of it, ∞ for a single root; the relative depth padicClusterRelValDepth is the difference with the parent's depth (∞ for a single root), and the depth for the top cluster (isPadicCluster\_rootSet). The committed real-valued padicClusterDepth and padicClusterRelDepth, with their junk values for single roots, are superseded by these. The model y² = f(x) enters through f, and p is any prime (odd for the LMFDB).
