* [`ag.cyclic_trigonal`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Background/Algebraic-geometry/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_ag___cyclic_trigonal_FLQQ_--statement) — Cyclic trigonal curve. Declarations (LeanBridge): `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IsCyclicTrigonalCurve`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IsTrigonalAutomorphism`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IsCyclicTrigonalSubgroup`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isCyclicTrigonalSubgroup_iff_forall`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isCyclicTrigonalCurve_iff_exists_isTrigonalAutomorphism`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isCyclicTrigonalCurve_projectiveLineOver`. Note: The model is replaced by the knowl's own definition: for X an object of Over (Spec K), IsCyclicTrigonalSubgroup H = Nat.card H = 3 and some quotient curve pi : X -\> Y of X by H (the committed IsQuotientCurve, which exists for every algebraic curve, committed in QuotientExistence.lean on 11-03, and is unique up to unique iso, so 'some' = 'every', isCyclicTrigonalSubgroup\_iff\_forall) has Y isomorphic over K to P\^1\_K (Tau Ceti's projectiveLine K as a scheme over K); IsCyclicTrigonalCurve X = some subgroup of Aut X is such; IsTrigonalAutomorphism sigma = zpowers sigma is such (generator of such an H), with the equivalence 'cyclic trigonal iff has a trigonal automorphism'. Automorphisms are those of X over K (g2c.aut\_grp). The affine line with x -\> zeta x is no longer an instance (A\^1/H = A\^1 is not P\^1). Concrete instance: over a field with a primitive cube root of unity zeta, P\^1 is cyclic trigonal (x -\> zeta x, fixed field K(x\^3), quotient isomorphic to P\^1 through Tau Ceti's anti-equivalence and the committed regular quotient), in particular over F\_7; for this, P\^1\_K is proved geometrically integral, hence an algebraic curve (ProjectiveLineCurve.lean). The committed function-field model IsCyclicTrigonalCurveOver (CyclicTrigonal.lean) is superseded and should not be linked; its docstrings still present it as the knowl's definition: replacement texts in review/AA3\_curves\_to