* [`ag.fq.point_counts`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Background/Algebraic-geometry/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_ag___fq___point_counts_FLQQ_--statement) — Point counts of a variety. Declarations (LeanBridge): `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.PointOver`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.finite_pointOver`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.finite_hom_spec_of_finiteType`. Note: The gap is closed: finite\_pointOver proves that a scheme X of finite type over a finite field K (LocallyOfFiniteType and QuasiCompact structure map; a variety over F\_q in particular) has finitely many L-points X.PointOver K L (morphisms Spec L -\> X over Spec K) for every finite extension L of K, so X(F\_q) (L = K) and X(F\_\{q\^n\}) are finite and Nat.card counts them without its junk value. Proof: X is compact, so finitely many charts of its affine open cover cover it; a morphism from the spectrum of a field factors through a chart containing its image point (IsOpenImmersion.lift), where it is the Spec of a ring map R\_j -\> L (Spec.preimage); R\_j is finitely generated over K (LocallyOfFiniteType through HasRingHomProperty.Spec\_iff), hence over Z as K is finite, and there are finitely many ring maps from a finitely generated ring to the finite ring L (finite\_ringHom\_of\_finiteType\_int).
* [`ag.geom_component`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Background/Algebraic-geometry/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_ag___geom_component_FLQQ_--statement) — Geometric component. Declarations (LeanBridge): `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.geometricComponents`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.geometricComponents_eq_range_connectedComponent`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.finite_geometricComponents`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.geometricGaloisPerm`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.irreducibleComponents_eq_range_connectedComponent`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.geometricBaseChangeScheme`. Note: Both gaps are closed. geometricComponents K X is the set of irreducible components of X\_Kbar = X x\_K Spec(AlgebraicClosure K) (geometricBaseChangeScheme, the scheme underlying LeanBridge's geometricBaseChange). The parenthetical fact: for X smooth and of finite type over K (Smooth and QuasiCompact structure map), geometricComponents\_eq\_range\_connectedComponent proves that they are exactly the connected components of X\_Kbar; the general theorem irreducibleComponents\_eq\_range\_connectedComponent (a Noetherian scheme smooth over a field) uses that connected components of a Noetherian space are open (Tau Ceti's local connectedness) and that a connected scheme smooth over a field is irreducible (Tau Ceti's Smooth.irreducibleSpace\_of\_connectedSpace). They are finitely many (finite\_geometricComponents: X\_Kbar is Noetherian). The Galois action: geometricGaloisPerm is a group homomorphism from Gal(Kbar/K) (Mathlib's Field.absoluteGaloisGroup K, by definition Kbar ≃ₐ\[K\] Kbar) to the permutations of the geometric components, sigma acting by preimage under the automorphism id x Spec(sigma) of the fibre product (geometricGaloisMap, a homeomorphism geometricGaloisHomeomorph with inverse that of sigma\^-1); a MulAction instance follows.
