ion\_polygon (not in this cluster, not recorded anywhere yet), old 'The slopes of the segments of \$P\$ are the' new 'The nonzero slopes of the segments of \$P\$ are the'. Readings, none open: the rams of E are Deligne's lower breaks (lf.rams's own definition); the family is defined by Deligne's upper breaks (ruling of 2026-11-13); I is at the residue characteristic of K (the knowl's 'p-adic family'). Neither of the two readings that AI6's review puts to the user for lf.family\_invariants (means, Artin slopes) is used here. Non-vacuity: every finite E inside K-bar has Herbrand invariant visibleHerbrandInvariant E (committed isInvariantOf\_visibleHerbrandInvariant), so the family theorems apply to every E (the review's ProbePolygon.lean). For lf.ramification\_polygon (no record here): see the review, care point 4. Changes by the review: the three statements named above; the author's private chord lemma TauCeti.IsConvexSeq.le\_affine\_of\_le\_of\_le (a convex sequence that is at most a line at two indices is at most it between them, 18 lines of real arithmetic) is removed: the step 'the hull is one line between two contact points' now goes through Tau Ceti's supporting faces, which are at the pin (TauCeti.IsSupportingLine and TauCeti.IsConvexSeq.ordConnected\_supportingFace, through the new lemma IsRamificationPolygon.isSupportingLine\_lowerConvexEnvelope, which replaces IsRamificationPolygon.ramificationLine\_le\_lowerConvexEnvelope), so RamificationPolygonHull.lean imports TauCeti.Analysis.Convex.Sequence.Face in place of TauCeti.Analysis.Convex.Sequence.Envelope; private helpers ram\_pos and mem\_Icc\_ramificationIndex\_of\_le\_of\_le and the lemma IsRamificationPolygon.lowerConvexEnvelope\_pow\_le in place of proof terms written two and three times; the hypothesis n in \[1, e\] of the lemma IsRamificationPolygon.lowerConvexEnvelope\_eq\_ramificationLine, which a supporting line valid at every index makes unnecessary, dropped; statements repacked. The general theor