e, and a comparison with Tau Ceti's HasGaloisLabel for polynomials. Blocked by: the user's ruling on the f \> 1 reading of equivalent residual polynomials (in a common subfamily, proved to mean classes up to Gal(K\_f/K)); an 'every member' reading would not give a reflexive relation for the review's example, and the partition would fail. Difficulty: none left in Lean (ruling only). Stale blockers: AO1's (1) the transport of the class of residual polynomials, (2) permutation-group isomorphism for subfields of K-bar and its invariance, (3) the invariance of the hidden slopes under K-isomorphism, all proved here. Review (AP2 reviewer, 2026-11-24; review/AP2\_transport.md): partial kept, pending the same ruling; the reviewer recommends formalised with the two text fixes. Every sentence of the live text (2025-06-26) checked: the setting (family, hp as for lf.subfamily), the definition and its five conditions, the Galois closures (Algebra.galoisClosure, the normal closure in K-bar), 'isomorphic as permutation groups' (Algebra.GaloisPermIsomorphic is the permutation isomorphism of the actions of the Galois groups on the K-embeddings, the action of nf.galois\_group; equal labels nTj give and are given by it for the LMFDB's fields, whose actions are faithful and transitive, facts of nf.galois\_group that lf.packet does not state), the residue field degree and ramification index of the closures, the hidden slopes (Swan, equivalently Artin) and 'Thus the family I/K is partitioned into packets' (isPartition\_packets). Nothing the knowl states is left out. The families paper (arXiv:2507.02360, section 4.1) defines packets by the Galois group and the hidden slope content alone; in its Table 4.1 each packet lies in one subfamily, and the LMFDB records packets per subfamily, so the knowl's added condition changes nothing there (not recorded). Text pair checked (old string once in the live text; a clarification that depends on the lf.subfamily fix). Decls trimmed to the eight to lin