* [`lf.ramification_polygon`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Fields/Local-fields/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_lf___ramification_polygon_FLQQ_--statement) — Ramification polygon. Declarations (LeanBridge): `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.ramificationPolynomial`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.ramificationPolygonOf`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.reflectedPolygon`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.isEisensteinAt_minpoly_unramifiedExtension`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.ramificationPolygonOf_eq_image_reflectVertical`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.ramificationPolygonOf_minpoly_eq_visibleHerbrandInvariant`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.IsInvariantOf.ramificationPolygonOf_minpoly`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.setOf_mem_segmentSlopes_ramificationPolygonOf_minpoly_ne_zero`. GitHub issues: [#64](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/64). Note: Round AJ (AJ6\_local\_fields). The three missing items of review/AI7\_finishing.md care point 4 and of the tracker blocker are closed, with the knowl's objects literally. Sentence by sentence (live text 2025-06-06). 'Let K'/K be the maximal unramified subextension of L/K. Then L/K' is totally ramified': K' = Tau Ceti's unramifiedExtension K L (inertiaDegree K L) (the unique intermediate field unramified over K with L totally ramified over it, eq\_unramifiedExtension\_inertiaDegree\_iff), TauCeti.isTotallyRamified\_unramifiedExtension\_inertiaDegree. 'if alpha in L is a uniformizer then the minimal polynomial phi(x) in K'\[x\] of alpha over K' will be Eisenstein': isEisensteinAt\_minpoly\_unramifiedExtension (the minimal polynomial over O\_\{K'\} of every uniformiser is Eisenstein; the minimal polynomial over the field K' is its image, Mathlib's minpoly.isIntegrallyClosed\_eq\_field\_fractions). 'the ramification polynomial rho(x) = alpha\^(-n) phi(alpha x + alpha) in L\[x\]': ramificationPolynomial phi alpha := C (alpha\^-1 \^ n) \* (phi.map).comp (C alpha \* X + C alpha), n = natDegree phi; 'Write rho(x) = x\^n + sum\_\{i\<n\} rho\_i x\^i': monic\_ramificationPolynomial, ramificationPolynomial\_eq\_X\_pow\_add\_sum, natDegree\_ramificationPolynomial (and coeff\_zero\_ramificationPolynomial: rho\_0 = 0). 'the ramification polygon of L/K is the lower convex hull of the set of points (-i, v\_L(rho\_i)), where we ignore all points with rho\_i = 0': ramificationPolygonOf phi alpha := lowerConvexHull (reflectVertical '' heightPoints (coeffHeight rho)), where lowerConvexHull S is the lower boundary of Mathlib's convexHull of S (new, LowerConvexHull.lean), coeffHeight rho n = v\_L(rho\_n) (normalised valuation, top for rho\_n = 0), and mem\_image\_reflectVertical\_heightPoints\_coeffHeight says the points are exactly the (-i, v\_L(rho\_i)) with rho\_i != 0; the leading coefficient rho\_n = 1 is a coefficient of rho, so its point (-n, 0) is among them (needed by the knowl's next sentence; AI7's question 5 for the editors stands). 'Thus the ramification polygon is the reflection of the Newton polygon of rho(x) through the vertical axis': ramificationPolygonOf\_eq\_image\_reflectVertical (the Newton polygon of lf.newton\_polygon being the lower convex hull of the points (i, v\_L(rho\_i)), rho\_i != 0), from lowerConvexHull\_image\_reflectVertical. 'This is independent of the choice of uniformizer alpha for L': ramificationPolygonOf\_minpoly\_eq\_visibleHerbrandInvariant (for every finite E inside K-bar of a p-adic field K and every uniformiser pi of E, the polygon of E/K at pi, with K' the maximal unramified subextension of E/K and phi = minpoly K' pi, is the polygon reflectedPolygon of the Herbrand invariant of E/K: the right side does not involve pi), ramificationPolygonOf\_minpoly\_eq\_of\_irreducible (two uniformisers give the same polygon), and in an abstract tower M/L/K with M/K finite Galois ramificationPolygonOf\_minpoly\_unramifiedExtension (= (herbrandInvariantOfTower K M L).reflectedPolygon). The proof: Monge's Proposition 1 and Lemma 1 for the minimal polynomial over O\_\{K'\} (committed IsMongeStage.isRamificationPolygon\_of\_hasSameRams with isMongeStage\_minpoly), AI7's IsRamificationPolygon.lowerConvexEnvelope\_eq (the Tau Ceti lower convex envelope of the heights is the polygon of the invariant), the new bridge lowerConvexHull\_heightPoints (for finitely many finite heights, the lower convex hull of the points (n, h\_n) is the graph of the piecewise-affine interpolation of Tau Ceti's lowerConvexEnvelope: the hull of Mathlib's convexHull equals the envelope), and coeffHeight\_ramificationPolynomial (the heights of the ramification polynomial are AI7's ramificationHeight). 'If I/K is a family ... the ramification polygon of I/K is defined to be the ramification polygon of any L/K in I/K': reflectedPolygon I (the reflection of AI7's ramificationPolygon I, through (-e, 0), (-p\^w, 0), (-p\^(w-k), e m\_k): mk\_neg\_ramificationIndex\_mem\_reflectedPolygon, mk\_neg\_pow\_mem\_reflectedPolygon) and HerbrandInvariant.IsInvariantOf.ramificationPolygonOf\_minpoly (for every E with Herbrand invariant I at the residue characteristic, i.e. every representative of every class of I/K by AI6's mk\_mem\_family\_iff, and every uniformiser, the polygon of E/K is reflectedPolygon I; via the new HasSameRams.ramificationPolygon\_eq). 'The slopes of the segments of P are the rams of L/K and I/K': with 'nonzero slopes' (text error recorded by AI7, old 'The slopes of the segments of \$P\$ are the' new 'The nonzero slopes of the segments of \$P\$ are the'; for eps \> 1 the polygon has the segment of slope 0 from (-e, 0) to (-p\^w, 0): checked in scratch ProbePolygon.lean on (3)\_2\^1, Q\_3(3\^(1/6)), 0 and 3 are segment slopes): setOf\_mem\_segmentSlopes\_ramificationPolygonOf\_minpoly\_ne\_zero (the nonzero slopes of the segments of the polygon of E/K at any uniformiser are the rams visibleRams E, Deligne's lower breaks) and HerbrandInvariant.setOf\_mem\_segmentSlopes\_reflectedPolygon\_ne\_zero (those of the polygon of I are r\_1..r\_w), segmentSlopes P being the slopes of the non-vertical nondegenerate segments contained in P, which by segmentSlopes\_polygonGraph are the slopes of the unit edges. Orientation: the polygon is drawn reflected as the LMFDB does (plot\_ramification\_polygon, lmfdb/local\_fields/main.py, clone f753c9a4e), so its slopes are +r\_k. Readings: p-adic field = CharZero K local field; the extensions are those inside K-bar (as for the families; the abstract tower statement covers any L inside a finite Galois M/K); v\_L normalised. Non-vacuity: every E has a uniformiser (exists\_irreducible) and a Herbrand invariant (ProbePolygon.lean). Checks as for lf.herbrand\_invariant (lint 0 errors, standard axioms, builds, no long line); simp deletion test (AG4's simpdel.py) on the three files: every entry needed after removing two smul\_eq\_mul entries of LowerConvexHull.lean. Tau Ceti main has Polynomial.newtonPolygon and lowerConvexEnvelope\_reflect; at the bump coeffHeight/lowerConvexEnvelope could be restated through them, nothing here needs main. Review (AJ6 reviewer, 2026-11-14; review/AJ6\_local\_fields.md): formalised, confirmed; the three items of AI7's care point 4 are closed. ramificationPolynomial is alpha\^(-n) phi(alpha x + alpha) literally, phi = minpoly over the field K' = unramifiedExtension K L (inertiaDegree K L), the unique intermediate field unramified over K with L totally ramified over it (Tau Ceti's eq\_unramifiedExtension\_inertiaDegree\_iff); ramificationPolygonOf is the lower boundary of Mathlib's convexHull of the points (-i, v\_L(rho\_i)), rho\_i != 0, the leading point (-n, 0) included (the reading AI7 sent to the editors: without it the hull of Q\_3(3\^(1/6)) ends with a segment of slope -3 up to (-5, 6), and the 'reflection of the Newton polygon of rho' sentence fails); reflectedPolygon is the reflection of AI7's explicit polygon of I; the bridge lowerConvexHull\_heightPoints (geometric hull = graph of the interpolated lowerConvexEnvelope, finitely many finite heights) was followed step by step. Checked on (3)\_2\^1 in the review's Probe.lean: (-6, 0), (-3, 0), (-1, 6) on the polygon, nothing at -7, segment slopes 0 and 3, nonzero slopes \{3\}. The 'Newton polygon of rho' is taken as the lower convex hull of lf.newton\_polygon although rho\_0 = 0 (that knowl assumes a\_0 a\_n != 0; the hull formula is what the text uses). Style fixes in the review (no statement changed): the left sides of ramificationPolygonOf\_minpoly\_unramifiedExtension and ramificationPolygonOf\_minpoly\_eq\_visibleHerbrandInvariant kept whole, mk\_neg\_pow\_mem\_reflectedPolygon, IsRamificationPolygon.ramificationPolygonOf\_eq and segmentSlopes\_reflectedPolygon repacked, two local statements repacked; lake build RamificationPolynomial 4.5 s, ExtensionRamificationPolygon 6.5 s, LowerConvexHull 6.6 s; simp deletion test re-run (all entries needed).
* [`lf.rams`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Fields/Local-fields/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_lf___rams_FLQQ_--statement) — Rams. Declarations (LeanBridge): `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.visibleRams`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.smallRam`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.tinyRam`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.mem_ramsOfIsGalois_iff_exists_addVal`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.IsInvariantOf.den_dvd_pow_ramMultiplicity_sub_one`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.mem_possibleRamSet_iff_exists_visibleRams_eq_replicate`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.finrank_ramSubextension_of_ram_lt`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.family_nonempty_iff_forall_mem_possibleRamSet`. GitHub issues: [#64](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/64). Note: Round AN (AN2\_heights\_rams), 2026-11-18. Formalised at the pin, with two corrections of the text (the degree of L\_i, the boundary of R\_1\^z), both proved in the corrected form. Setting: K a nonarchimedean local field, L/K finite separable inside K-bar; the possible rams over K are for K of characteristic 0 (the knowl's p-adic fields), with p the residue characteristic and e\_0 = v\_K(p) = e\_K. This closes the sweep record ZX2 ('No lemma bounds the denominator of a ram by p\^k - 1 or produces intermediate fields at strict increases ... ramSet is only defined and is used nowhere else'). Sentence by sentence. (1) The rams, small rams and tiny rams and the two relations: committed (visibleRams, ramsOfSubgroup, visibleRams\_eq\_ramsOfIsGalois; smallRam, tinyRam, smallRam\_eq\_mean\_sub\_mean, tinyRam\_eq\_swanSlope\_sub\_mean). (2) 'When L/K is Galois a ram is any number of the form v\_L(sigma(pi\_L) - pi\_L) - 1 for some sigma != 1 in the wild inertia group ... Thus the rams of a Galois extension are positive integers': GaloisRamsUniformizer.lean, mem\_ramsOfIsGalois\_iff\_exists\_addVal (for a uniformiser pi of L, n is a ram iff v\_L(sigma pi - pi) = n + 1 for some sigma != 1 in G\_1, the wild inertia group), with lowerIndex\_eq\_addVal\_smul\_sub (i\_G(sigma) = v\_L(sigma pi - pi) for sigma in G\_0) and mem\_ramsOfIsGalois\_iff (n is a ram iff n \>= 1 and G\_(n+1) != G\_n). (3) 'in general a ram may have denominator dividing p\^k - 1 where k is the multiplicity of the ram': IsInvariantOf.den\_dvd\_pow\_ramMultiplicity\_sub\_one (the denominator of a ram of multiplicity k divides p\^k - 1; from round AJ's den\_pow\_ramMultiplicity\_sub\_one\_mul), and the bound is attained: exists\_visibleRams\_eq\_replicate\_inv (a totally ramified extension of degree p\^w whose w rams are all 1/(p\^w - 1)). (4) The sets R\_k\^z: possibleRamSet p k z (PossibleRamSet.lean), the positive rationals with denominator dividing p\^k - 1, numerator prime to p and alpha \< pz/(p - 1), together with pz/(p - 1) when k = 1; mem\_possibleRamSet\_iff ((p\^k - 1) alpha is an integer prime to p); natCast\_mul\_div\_notMem\_ramSet, ramSet\_eq\_setOf and possibleRamSet\_eq\_ramSet\_union compare it with the committed ramSet (the knowl as written): for natural z the boundary value pz/(p - 1) is never in the knowl's R\_1\^z, its numerator being divisible by p, so the knowl's '\<=' is a '\<', and possibleRamSet is ramSet together with that value for k = 1. (5) 'The possible rams r\_1 = ... = r\_w for totally wildly ramified extensions of degree p\^w over K are then just given by R\_w\^(e\_K)': mem\_possibleRamSet\_iff\_exists\_visibleRams\_eq\_replicate (for w \>= 1, alpha lies in the corrected R\_w\^(e\_0) iff some totally ramified extension E/K of degree p\^w inside K-bar has visibleRams E = w copies of alpha), both directions; exists\_visibleRams\_eq\_singleton\_arithmetic (the boundary value p e\_0/(p - 1) is the ram of a totally ramified extension of degree p, so the correction is needed). (6) 'if r\_i \< r\_(i+1) then L/K has an intermediate field L\_i with \[L\_i:K\] = eps p\^i': relfinrank\_ramSubextension\_ram (\[L\_i : K\_f\] = eps p\^i for L\_i = L\^(r\_i), at every vertex i) and finrank\_ramSubextension\_of\_ram\_lt (\[L\_i : K\] = f eps p\^i); the knowl's degree eps p\^i over K is right for f = 1 only. (7) 'the possible rams (r\_1, ..., r\_w) over K are chosen sequentially' and 'each r\_k is chosen from R\_1\^(e\_K eps p\^(k-1))': family\_nonempty\_iff\_forall\_mem\_possibleRamSet (the invariant (r\_1, ..., r\_w)\_eps\^f occurs over K iff each distinct ram b, of multiplicity d and with c smaller rams, lies in the corrected R\_d\^(e\_0 eps p\^c)) and family\_nonempty\_iff\_of\_ram\_lt (for r\_1 \< ... \< r\_w, iff r\_k lies in R\_1\^(e\_0 eps p\^(k-1)) for 1 \<= k \<= w); also family\_nonempty\_iff\_isCompatible and family\_nonempty\_iff\_isCompatibleWith (the family I/K is nonempty iff I is compatible with K, the converse of lf.herbrand\_invariant's necessary conditions). Route of the existence: CompatibleAdmissible.lean proves IsCompatible.isAdmissible (compatible implies Monge's admissibility, by induction over the vertices: e m\_k = p\^(w-k)(p\^d B + N) with N = (p\^d - 1) b), so isAdmissible\_iff\_isCompatible; ExtensionFamilyNonempty.lean proves isInvariantOf\_of\_eval₂\_specialisation\_eq\_zero (a root in K-bar of a specialisation of the generic polynomial of an admissible invariant over the unramified extension F of degree f, with unit coefficients at the D- and A-points, generates over F an extension with that invariant: the committed hasSameRams\_of\_specialisation) and takes all coefficients 1 (IsAdmissible.family\_nonempty). Text errors. (a) The degree: old 'then \$L/K\$ has an intermediate field \$L\_i\$ with \$\[L\_i:K\] = \\epsilon p\^i\$.' (once in the live text), new 'then \$L/K\$ has an intermediate field \$L\_i\$ with \$\[L\_i:K\_f\] = \\epsilon p\^i\$, where \$K\_f/K\$ is the maximal unramified subextension of \$L/K\$.' (equivalently \$\[L\_i:K\] = f\\epsilon p\^i\$; lf.means writes \$K\_f\$ too). The brief's counterexample for f \> 1 is right for odd p = 2 mod 3 and was checked by hand only (not in Lean): K = Q\_p, u a non-cube unit of Q\_(p\^2), L = Q\_(p\^2)((up)\^(1/(3p\^2))) has f = 2, eps = 3, rams 3p/(p - 1) \< 3p\^2/(p - 1) and no subfield of degree 3p over Q\_p. For p = 2 the argument's last step fails (\[E : K\_f\] = 3p/2 = 3 is an integer, and Q\_4(cuberoot(2u)) itself has degree 6 = eps p over Q\_2). (b) The boundary: old '\\mathcal\{R\}\_1\^\{z\} = \\left\\\{\\alpha \\in \\mathcal\{R\}\_1\^\\infty : \\alpha \\le \\frac\{pz\}\{p-1\}\\right\\\}', new '\\mathcal\{R\}\_1\^\{z\} = \\left\\\{\\alpha \\in \\mathcal\{R\}\_1\^\\infty : \\alpha \< \\frac\{pz\}\{p-1\}\\right\\\} \\cup \\left\\\{\\frac\{pz\}\{p-1\}\\right\\\}'. Proposed change of the committed ramSet (HerbrandInvariantRams.lean, used nowhere else): give it the body of possibleRamSet, \{alpha \| 0 \< alpha and (alpha.den dvd p\^k - 1 and not p dvd alpha.num and alpha \< p z/(p - 1), or k = 1 and alpha = p z/(p - 1))\}, with the docstring of possibleRamSet. Readings: 'totally wildly ramified of degree p\^w' is IsTotallyRamified K E with \[E : K\] = p\^w; 'possible rams over K' is (I.family K).Nonempty; the wild inertia group of a Galois L/K is G\_1 (Tau Ceti's ramificationGroupOneSylow, linked to lf.wild\_inertia\_group). Further declarations for the links, beyond the eight: IsInvariantOf.den\_dvd\_pow\_ramMultiplicity\_sub\_one, family\_nonempty\_iff\_of\_ram\_lt, relfinrank\_ramSubextension\_ram, exists\_visibleRams\_eq\_singleton\_arithmetic, smallRam\_eq\_mean\_sub\_mean, tinyRam\_eq\_swanSlope\_sub\_mean. Checks: lake build of the five modules, \#lint clean, axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. Unproved: only the counterexample of (a), by hand. Review (AN2 reviewer, 2026-11-18; review/AN2\_heights\_rams.md): formalised, confirmed, with the two corrections, both fixable errors (ruling of 2026-11-11): each replaces a false statement by the true one, which is proved in full, and drops no true claim. Every sentence of the live text (2025-05-28) checked against the Lean, those proved in earlier rounds included. The existence theorem followed step by step: IsCompatible.isAdmissible (induction over the vertices; a geometric block gives e m\_k = p\^(w-k)(p\^d B + N) with p not dividing N, an arithmetic one the small ram e\_0) and the committed hasSameRams\_of\_specialisation, whose hypotheses are met for every compatible invariant, every f and every eps (all coefficients 1 over the unramified extension of degree f); no nonemptiness hypothesis enters, so there is no circularity. Non-vacuity (scratch AN2\_heights\_rams-review/Probe.lean): (2)\_1\^1 at p = 2, (3)\_2\^1 at p = 3 and (15/4, 75/4)\_3\^2 at p = 5 are compatible with e\_K = 1, and their families are not empty over every K of that residue characteristic with v\_K(p) = 1. (b) The boundary, checked in Lean and by hand: over Q\_2 the totally ramified quartic fields have c in \{4, 6, 8\} for one block (rams 1/3, 1, 5/3; the pair (2, 2) does not occur) and c in \{8, 9, 10, 11\} for two ((1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4)), and over Q\_3 the totally ramified cubic fields have rams 1/2, 1, 3/2 (c = 3, 4, 5); without the boundary value Q\_2(sqrt 2), Q\_3(cuberoot 3) and Q\_2(2\^(1/4)) would be missing. (a) The degree: the counterexample checked step by step for p = 5 mod 6, with a second argument for its key step (Q\_(p\^2)(cuberoot(up)) is not Galois over Q\_p, as Frob(u)/u is not a cube, while Q\_(p\^2)(cuberoot p) is, so the former has no cubic subfield); for p = 5 the invariant is (15/4, 75/4)\_3\^2 and every member has \[L\_1 : K\] = 30, not 15 (Probe.lean). The committed ramSet: keep its body (the knowl's literal set, on which the three comparison theorems rest) and change its docstring to say so and to point to possibleRamSet; exact texts in the review. decls changed by the review: IsInvariantOf.den\_dvd\_pow\_ramMultiplicity\_sub\_one (the denominator sentence) is linked and possibleRamSet no longer is (it is named in the statements of the two linked theorems on possible rams); the author's list is the alternative. Otherwise style fixes only (review, section Changes): no statement of a linked declaration changed.
* [`lf.residual_polynomials`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Fields/Local-fields/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_lf___residual_polynomials_FLQQ_--statement) — Residual polynomials. Declarations (LeanBridge): `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.residualPolynomial`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.residualPolynomials`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.residualPolynomialClass`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.mem_integer_coeff_ramificationPolynomial`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.mem_polygonEdges_ramificationPolygonOf_iff`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.aeval_add_X_pow_mul_comp_residualPolynomial`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.PadicCbrtThree.residualPolynomials_neg_cbrtThree_ne`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.residualPolynomialClass_eq_of_irreducible_of_charZero`, `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.residualPolynomialClass_minpoly_algEquiv`. Note: Round AO (AO1\_residual\_polynomials), 2026-11-23. Formalised, with one fixable text issue (the order of S\_1, ..., S\_l). Every statement of the knowl is proved for a totally ramified extension L/K of p-adic fields (more generally of nonarchimedean local fields with L/K separable; the CharZero corollary covers p-adic fields), alpha a uniformiser, phi its minimal polynomial over K, v\_alpha = addValuation L (v(alpha) = 1), rho = ramificationPolynomial phi alpha (committed). (1) rho in O\_L\[x\]: mem\_integer\_coeff\_ramificationPolynomial. (2) The segments S with endpoints (-k-l, v(rho\_\{k+l\})), (-k, v(rho\_k)) and slope h/m are exactly the segments of the ramification polygon (mem\_polygonEdges\_ramificationPolygonOf\_iff, on residualSegments, read off Tau Ceti's lowerConvexEnvelope; the ends are points by EdgeOfSlopeEnds.lean). (3) A(x) = sum\_\{j=0\}\^\{l/m\} red(rho\_\{jm+k\} alpha\^\{jh - v(rho\_k)\}) x\^j exactly as written (residualPolynomial; the reduced elements lie in O\_L: mem\_integer\_residualPolynomial; degree l/m and nonzero constant term: natDegree\_residualPolynomial, coeff\_zero\_residualPolynomial\_ne\_zero). (4) For S of positive slope, x\^k A(x\^m) is additive: its coefficients vanish away from the powers of p (coeff\_X\_pow\_mul\_comp\_residualPolynomial\_eq\_zero, through Monge's binomial argument v(rho\_s) \<= v(rho\_i) for s = p\^\{v\_p(i)\}, coeffVal\_pow\_padicValNat\_le) and B(x+y) = B(x)+B(y) in every commutative algebra over the residue field, polynomial rings included (aeval\_add\_X\_pow\_mul\_comp\_residualPolynomial); no separability needed. (5) The list residualPolynomials, S\_1 at the right. (6) 'The list ... is not an invariant': Q\_3(3\^(1/3)) (the lead's example, LeanBridge.PadicRadical 3 3 = AdjoinRoot (X\^3 - 3), its lemmas in the namespace PadicCbrtThree): the single segment (k,l) = (1,2) of slope 3/2 (residualSegments\_eq), lists \[1 + x\] at alpha and \[2 + x\] at -alpha (residualPolynomials\_cbrtThree, residualPolynomials\_neg\_cbrtThree), which differ (residualPolynomials\_neg\_cbrtThree\_ne). (7) The class A = \{(gamma\_\{d,1\} A\_1(d\^\{h\_1\} x), ..., gamma\_\{d,l\} A\_l(d\^\{h\_l\} x)) : d in K\_\^x\} with the knowl's recursion gamma\_\{d,l\} = d\^(-h\_l deg A\_l), gamma\_\{d,i\} = gamma\_\{d,i+1\} d\^(-h\_i deg A\_i) (residualGammas, residualAct, residualPolynomialClass, d mapped into the residue field of L), and 'A is an invariant of K\[x\]/(phi)': the class does not depend on the uniformiser (residualPolynomialClass\_eq\_of\_irreducible, separable; residualPolynomialClass\_eq\_of\_irreducible\_of\_charZero for p-adic fields), with the list at alpha' inside the class at alpha (residualPolynomials\_mem\_residualPolynomialClass) and the explicit change A'\_S(x) = u\_\^(-v(rho\_k)) A\_S(u\_\^h x) for alpha' = u alpha (residualPolynomial\_eq\_of\_irreducible, Pauli-Sinclair Lemma 4.7); the knowl's gamma\_\{d,i\} is d\^(-v(rho\_\{k\_i\})) (residualAct\_residualPairs). Route (Monge's invariance proof, MongeInvariance.lean): in the normal closure M of L/K inside an algebraic closure (Tau Ceti's finite intermediate field structures), phi(alpha + alpha x) = prod over Gal(M/K)/Gal(M/L) of (alpha - s alpha + alpha x) (committed map\_eq\_prod\_quotient, map\_mongeShift\_eq\_prod); each factor of phi'(alpha' + alpha' x) differs from u times the factor of phi by s(alpha)(u - s u), divisible by alpha(s alpha - alpha) (committed smul\_sub\_dvd\_smul\_algebraMap\_sub); Mathlib's Gauss norm (multiplicative for a nonarchimedean absolute value, any real c \> 0) gives \|\|F' - F\|\| \< \|\|F\|\| for the products (Polynomial.gaussNorm\_prod\_sub\_prod\_lt), i.e. every point of rho' - rho lies strictly above every supporting line of rho at every real slope (exists\_coeffVal\_sub\_lt); so the Newton polygons agree (coeffEnvelope\_eq\_of\_forall) and on each segment the coefficients agree to first order (residualPolynomial\_mul\_eq). Monge's comparison only covers the integer slopes m; rational slopes h/m need the real Gauss norm, hence the new addValAbs (x -\> 2\^(-v(x))). Numerical tests before writing (scratch/AO1\_residual\_polynomials/residual\_test.py): five examples, the lead's first and Pauli-Sinclair's Example 4.9, whose class is reproduced exactly (their base list is ours at -alpha). TEXT (fixable, ambiguous order): the knowl never says how S\_1, ..., S\_l are numbered, and the gamma recursion depends on it: it is right with S\_1 the rightmost segment (Pauli-Sinclair's numbering, S\_l ending at (-n, 0)), where gamma\_\{d,i\} = d\^(-v(rho\_\{k\_i\})) by telescoping (consecutive segments share ends, the last ends at height 0); numbered from the left, gamma\_\{d,l\} would be d\^(-(v(rho\_1) - v(rho\_\{1+l\}))) instead of the d\^(-v(rho\_1)) of the change of uniformiser. Old (live text of 2025-05-15, occurs once): 'The \*\*residual polynomials\*\* of \$\\varphi\$ are the residual polynomials associated to the segments \$S\_1, \\dots, S\_\\ell\$ of the \{\{KNOWL('lf.ramification\_polygon', 'ramification polygon')\}\} of \$\\varphi\$.' New: 'The \*\*residual polynomials\*\* of \$\\varphi\$ are the residual polynomials associated to the segments \$S