f that over L\^un of alpha, and the class of residual polynomials is the image under the residue map of sigma (residualPolynomialClass\_minpoly\_algEquiv); the action of the residue units composes (residualAct\_residualAct) and the class over a field onto whose residue field the base surjects is an orbit (residualPolynomialClass\_eq\_residualActOrbit). Family (ResidualPolynomialTransportFamily.lean): for a member E of I/K the residue map of K\_f \<= E is an isomorphism (IsInvariantOf.residueFieldEquiv); the class of E at alpha read over the residue field of K\_f (IsInvariantOf.residualClass) is an orbit of the residue units (residualClass\_eq\_residualActOrbit) and independent of the uniformiser (residualClass\_eq\_of\_irreducible); for a K-isomorphism sigma : E = E' of members it changes by the automorphism of the residue field induced by the restriction of sigma to K\_f (residualClass\_algEquiv, pairs: residualPairsOver\_algEquiv), a power of Frobenius x -\> x\^(q\^n) (exists\_residueFieldHom\_eq\_pow), and every element of Gal(K\_f/K) arises from a K-isomorphism onto another member (exists\_restrictUnramifiedExtension\_eq). Consequences: E lies in the subfamily of the class A0 of a member E0 iff its class is the image of A0 under an element of Gal(K\_f/K) (mk\_mem\_subfamily\_residualClass\_iff); (a) for f = 1 the literal condition holds at any member and any uniformiser (mk\_mem\_subfamily\_residualClass\_iff\_of\_f\_eq\_one); (b) for every f the condition up to Gal(K\_f/K) holds at any member and any uniformiser (mk\_mem\_galoisSubfamily\_residualClass\_iff); the subfamily of the image of A under any element of Gal(K\_f/K) is the subfamily of A (subfamily\_image\_map\_residueFieldHom); the subfamilies of the classes of the members partition I/K, for every f (isPartition\_subfamilies). Hypothesis throughout the family results: ringChar of the residue field of K is p (I at the residue characteristic, as for the LMFDB's families); it gives equal slopes to all members. Finding against the AO1 review: under 'some member, some uniformiser' the review's example does not lie in two subfamilies; the subfamilies of a class and of its Frobenius image are the same set (subfamily\_image\_map\_residueFieldHom) and the subfamilies partition I/K (isPartition\_subfamilies); 'some member' and 'up to Gal(K\_f/K)' coincide, and only 'every member' fails (the example would lie in no subfamily). LMFDB checked: lf.field.label gives each field one code i 'shared among fields in the same family with equivalent residual polynomials'; ctr\_subfamily is data; rcs.cande.lf: all extensions of Q\_p of degree n \< 24 with p \< 200, so the review's octic example (Q\_2, f = 2, e = 4) is in the database; residual polynomials are stored data. Text error (fixable, reading (b); the reviewer's wording, which names the extension L/K\_f whose residual polynomials are meant): old 'whose list of residual polynomials is in \$\\mathcal\{A\}\$.' (once in knowls\_live.json) new 'whose list of residual polynomials over the unramified extension \$K\_f\$ of \$K\$ of degree \$f\$ is in \$\\mathcal\{A\}\$ up to the action of \$\\Gal(K\_f/K)\$ on the coefficients.' Not formalised: the review's octic example over Q\_2(zeta\_3) (not cheap; it shows that a class need not be Frobenius-stable, which only the 'every member' reading needs). Blocked by: the user's ruling on the f \> 1 reading of 'whose list of residual polynomials is in A' (some member, equivalently up to Gal(K\_f/K): proved; every member: not the LMFDB's partition); with the text fix accepted, formalised. Difficulty: none left in Lean (ruling only). Stale blockers: AO1's (1) the transport along K-isomorphisms inside K-bar and (2) the independence of the uniformiser within I/K, both proved here. Review (AP2 reviewer, 2026-11-24; review/AP2\_transport.md): partial kept, pending the user's ruling; the reviewer recommends formalised with the text fix (question in the review). Checked: the transport (residualPolynomialClass\_minpoly\_algEquiv, for every K-isomorphism of finite extensions of a nonarchimedean local field; its redundant FiniteDimensional hypothesis on the target removed), the twist (IsInvariantOf.residualClass\_algEquiv, any element alpha, no hypothesis on p), Frobenius (exists\_residueFieldHom\_eq\_pow), every element of Gal(K\_f/K) arising (exists\_restrictUnramifiedExtension\_eq), the orbit algebra (residualAct\_residualAct, residualClass\_eq\_residualActOrbit) and the consequences. hp : ringChar k\_K = p is the LMFDB's setting (I is a Herbrand invariant at the residue characteristic of K: lf.herbrand\_invariant, lf.family\_polynomial; committed precedent IsInvariantOf.ramificationPolygonOf\_minpoly and round AI6's review), used only to give two members the same slopes; the transport, the twist, subfamily\_eq\_galoisSubfamily and subfamily\_image\_map\_residueFieldHom do not use it. The finding against the AO1 review is right: the octic's two classes (recomputed with AO1's resid\_check.py: list (zeta + x, 1 + x\^2); the Frobenius-conjugate polynomial's list (zeta\^2 + x, 1 + x\^2) is outside the class) give one subfamily as a set; for f \> 1 only the injectivity of A -\> subfamily(A) and the 'every member' reading fail. LMFDB: its code computes no subfamily (ctr\_subfamily is stored and used in sort orders only); stored residual polynomials have coefficients in Z\[t\] (main.py, plot\_ramification\_polygon: R = ZZ\['t'\]\['z'\]), t the residue generator of the stored K\_f, so for f \> 1 a stored list depends on the chosen K\_f-structure of the field; the families paper (arXiv:2507.02360) works with f = 1 (section 3) and defers f \> 1. Decls trimmed to the eight to link; also relevant: subfamilies, mk\_mem\_subfamily\_residualClass\_iff, IsInvariantOf.residualClass\_algEquiv, exists\_residueFieldHom\_eq\_pow, residualPolynomialClass\_minpoly\_algEquiv (ResidualPolynomialTransport), subfamily\_subset\_family (ExtensionSubfamily), family, residualPolynomialClass, res