* [`nf.ideal_labels`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Fields/Number-fields/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_nf___ideal_labels_FLQQ_--statement) — Ideal labels. Declarations (LeanBridge): `NumberField.lmfdbIdealLabel`, `NumberField.idealLabel`, `NumberField.IdealLT`, `NumberField.idealLabel_injective`, `NumberField.primeKey`, `NumberField.padicFactor`. Note: Formalised the Cremona-Page-Sutherland order (arXiv:2005.09491, sections 2-3; conventions checked against psort.py of github.com/JohnCremona/Sorting) for an integral primitive element alpha: primes by norm, ramification index and the lexicographic order of the p-adic digit vector (a\_\{0,0\}, a\_\{1,0\}, ..., a\_\{0,1\}, ...) of their p-adic factor (the minimal polynomial over Q\_p of alpha in K\_P, proved irreducible, dividing g, of degree e\*f and with Z\_p coefficients), and the ideals of norm N lexicographically on their p-parts, each compared by weight and then by the reverse lexicographic order of the exponents. Proved that distinct primes above p have distinct p-adic factors (via Tau Ceti's semilocal decomposition Q\_p (x) K = prod K\_P), that the order is a strict total order on primes and on ideals, that the label N.i (the existing Ideal.normLabel) is injective with values exactly N.1, ..., N.m, and that prime ideals come first among the ideals of their norm and are ordered as the primes. The LMFDB's alpha is the class of X in Q\[X\]/(g), g = NumberField.polredabs K (nf.polredabs, formalised), proved integral and primitive, which gives NumberField.lmfdbIdealLabel (injective); for an abstract K the labels depend on the isomorphism Q\[X\]/(g) = K only up to an automorphism of K, as the knowl's 'canonical alpha' presupposes K = Q\[X\]/(g).
