te Hausdorff monoid) and IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.finite\_continuousMonoidHom\_absoluteGaloisGroup (every finite extension K of Q\_p), specialised to K = Q\_p. The core of the suggested route, finitely many extensions of degree n inside K-bar, is proved too as a corollary, though the knowl does not need it: IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.finite\_setOf\_finrank\_eq (n != 0; fixing subgroups are open of index n by Mathlib's fixingSubgroup\_isOpen and finrank\_eq\_fixingSubgroup\_index, a topologically finitely generated group has finitely many open subgroups of each index by Tau Ceti's finite\_openSubgroup\_index\_eq\_of\_ne\_zero, and L -\> fixingSubgroup L is injective by Mathlib's Galois coinsertion InfiniteGalois.GaloisCoinsertionIntermediateFieldSubgroup). Sentence by sentence: weight function (NumberField.WeightFunction, with the recorded 'n coprime to \#G'); H\_\{w,p\} = p\^\{w(phi(tau\_p))\} (localHeight), independent of the generator tau\_p (localHeight\_eq) and positive (localHeight\_pos); the finite set Hom(Gamma\_Qp, G) (new); H the product of the local heights (inertialHeight), a finite product (finite\_mulSupport\_inertialHeight), positive for positive H\_p (inertialHeight\_pos); the radical-discriminant example (inertialHeight\_indicator\_eq\_finprod\_ramifiedPrimes, through forall\_apply\_map\_eq\_one\_iff\_notMem\_ramifiedPrimes and finprod\_mem\_ramifiedPrimes\_eq\_prod\_primeFactors); the last sentence is a remark with the recorded placeholder. Links: the new theorem takes the place of NumberField.forall\_apply\_map\_eq\_one\_iff\_notMem\_ramifiedPrimes (InertialHeightRamification), the bridge behind the example, to stay at eight; it remains available, with localHeight\_pos and finprod\_mem\_ramifiedPrimes\_eq\_prod\_primeFactors. Build note for the merge: the new module imports Tau Ceti's Generation.AbsoluteGaloisGroup, outside LeanBridge's import closure until now; its first build compiled 206 and unpacked 79 Tau Ceti modules (about 31 minutes of summed compile time), none of them in the closure of LeanBridge.lean, so no committed module went stale. Recorded edits stand (is a a function; n coprime to \#G; p\^\{w(phi(tau\_p))\}; second product over p not dividing \#G; the placeholder 'See ??? for further details'). No new text error. Review (AH2): every step checked, formalised confirmed. Tau Ceti's isTopologicallyFinitelyGenerated\_absoluteGaloisGroup (pin 5a01f5fe) is about Mathlib's Field.absoluteGaloisGroup K with its Krull topology; at K = Q\_\[p\] the new theorem's type is, instance for instance, the domain of inertialHeight's H p (pp.explicit, and unification at reducible-and-instances transparency); the theorem's 872-module Tau Ceti import closure has no sorry, admit, axiom, opaque or native\_decide in code, and \#print axioms on it, on the four new lemmas and on the linked lemmas gives propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound only. The T2 hypothesis covers the committed discrete G (a finite Hausdorff group is discrete; the committed definition takes any topology, its theorems the discrete one). Changes: the import TauCeti.Topology.Algebra.Group.OpenSubgroup.TopologicallyFinitelyGenerated removed (redundant: in the closure of the other import and already in that of LeanBridge.lean); docstrings say 'finite Hausdorff group'; the injectivity step of finite\_setOf\_finrank\_eq uses the Galois coinsertion. Cost: CI fetches Tau Ceti from its public cache (the pin's revision mapping has 15755 entries, as many as its modules; no CI log shows a Tau Ceti module built), so the 285 Tau Ceti modules the new import adds are downloaded once per workflow (about 445 MiB of outputs), not compiled; no lighter import exists (269 of the 285 are needed by the finite generation proof itself, 15 come from GeneratorRank). dup\_decls: 0 clashes over 16101 modules.
