* [`nf.nickname`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Fields/Number-fields/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_nf___nickname_FLQQ_--statement) — Number field nicknames. Declarations (Mathlib · LeanBridge · Tau Ceti): `IsCyclotomicExtension`, `NumberField.maximalRealSubfield`, `IsPrimitiveRoot.maximalRealSubfield_eq_adjoin_add_inv`, `IsPrimitiveRoot.add_inv_mem_maximalRealSubfield`, `TauCeti.IsCyclotomicExtension.Rat.toSubfield_fixedField_zpowers_galEquivZMod_symm_neg_one`. Note: Round AI (AI2), reviewed. Formalised. The nicknames themselves (Q, Qi, QsqrtN, QzetaN, QzetaN+, Q(s1, ..., sk), and the sqrt, root, cbrt, zetaN, phi syntax with its examples) are a site convention: 'Q(sqrt N)', 'zeta\_N is a primitive Nth root of unity' and 'phi (for (1 + sqrt 5)/2)' only say what the names denote and assert nothing. The one mathematical statement is in 'QzetaN+, for Q(zeta\_N)\^+; i.e. the maximal real subfield of Q(zeta\_N) (equivalently, the field Q(zeta\_N + zeta\_N\^\{-1\}))': the maximal real subfield of Q(zeta\_N) is Q(zeta\_N + zeta\_N\^\{-1\}). Q(zeta\_N) is any K with Mathlib's IsCyclotomicExtension \{N\} Q K, a number field, for example Mathlib's CyclotomicField N Q or the subfield of C generated by the N-th roots of unity. Its maximal real subfield is Mathlib's NumberField.maximalRealSubfield, the elements real under every complex embedding, which is the largest totally real subfield (Mathlib's isTotallyReal\_iff\_le\_maximalRealSubfield). New, IsPrimitiveRoot.maximalRealSubfield\_eq\_adjoin\_add\_inv: for every primitive N-th root of unity zeta in K, every N \>= 1 (N = 1 and N = 2, where both sides are K = Q, included), maximalRealSubfield K = (Q⟮zeta + zeta⁻¹⟯).toSubfield. Proof, without galEquivZMod: (i) zeta + zeta\^\{-1\} is real under every embedding phi, as \|phi zeta\| = 1 makes (phi zeta)\^\{-1\} its conjugate (IsPrimitiveRoot.add\_inv\_mem\_maximalRealSubfield); (ii) K/Q is Galois (Mathlib's IsCyclotomicExtension.isGalois), so Q(zeta + zeta\^\{-1\}) is the fixed field of its fixing subgroup (IsGalois.fixedField\_fixingSubgroup). An automorphism sigma fixing zeta + zeta\^\{-1\} satisfies (sigma zeta - zeta)(sigma zeta - zeta\^\{-1\}) = 0. Either sigma = 1 (it agrees with the identity on the generator zeta), or sigma zeta = zeta\^\{-1\}, and then phi o sigma = conj o phi for every complex embedding phi, so sigma fixes the maximal real subfield. Tau Ceti's TauCeti.IsCyclotomicExtension.Rat.toSubfield\_fixedField\_zpowers\_galEquivZMod\_symm\_neg\_one (the maximal real subfield is the fixed field of zeta -\> zeta\^\{-1\}) is linked as the companion description. No text error. Review: statement and proof checked; no statement changed (two inline extensionality proofs shortened with Set.eqOn\_singleton). Non-vacuity (scratch Probe.lean): the theorem applies to CyclotomicField n Q for every n \>= 1 and for n = 1, 2 (Mathlib's instance CyclotomicField.isCyclotomicExtension n Q given explicitly; inferInstance does not find it at this pin), and to IntermediateField.adjoin Q \{b : C \| b \^ n = 1\} through the committed instances of MulChar/GaloisAction.lean. lake build through the guard; \#lint (15 linters) clean; axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound; both simp lemmas needed (deletion test); the three public names are new in Mathlib, Tau Ceti and LeanBridge.
