* [`nf.picture`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Fields/Number-fields/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_nf___picture_FLQQ_--statement) — Pictures for number fields. Declarations (Mathlib · LeanBridge): `PrimeSpectrum`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isoSpec`, `MvPolynomial.zeroLocusToMaximalSpectrum`, `MvPolynomial.bijective_zeroLocusToMaximalSpectrum`, `Ideal.primesOver`, `PrimeSpectrum.preimage_comap_singleton_eq_primesOver`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.fiber`, `NumberField.range_fiberι_spec_map_algebraMap_int`. Note: Round AI (AI2), reviewed. Formalised under either reading of its one ambiguous sentence; no confirmed text error, one question for the editors. The drawing conventions (points, colours, radii, connecting lines, where Spec Z is drawn) are display. Two mathematical remarks. (1) 'points on a curve over \$\\mathbb\{C\}\$ are in bijection with prime ideals of its coordinate ring'. Review's reading: the knowl is written in the language of schemes (the prime spectrum of O\_F 'visualized as a curve over Spec Z', 'Each prime ideal in Spec O\_F is drawn as a point', the fibres of Spec O\_F -\> Spec Z), and the LMFDB's picture marks the generic point (0) on Spec O\_F and on Spec Z (lmfdb/number\_fields/draw\_spectrum.py). For the points of an affine curve as a scheme the sentence is true and is Mathlib's definition of Spec: the points of Spec A are the prime ideals of A (PrimeSpectrum; (Spec A : Type) = PrimeSpectrum A by rfl), and an affine scheme is the spectrum of its coordinate ring (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isoSpec). For the points of the curve in C\^n (the LMFDB's own ag.variety is classical) the sentence is false as written: the zero ideal of the coordinate ring of an irreducible curve is prime and is no point; the true statement is with the maximal ideals, old 'are in bijection with prime ideals of its coordinate ring', new 'are in bijection with maximal ideals of its coordinate ring'. That statement is proved for every affine variety over every algebraically closed field (curves over C included): MvPolynomial.bijective\_zeroLocusToMaximalSpectrum. For an ideal I of K\[X\_s : s in sigma\], sigma finite, the map MvPolynomial.zeroLocusToMaximalSpectrum, sending a point x of V(I) to the kernel of the evaluation at x on K\[X\] / I, is a bijection onto MaximalSpectrum (K\[X\] / I); with I the defining ideal of a variety, K\[X\] / I is its coordinate ring. The proof uses Mathlib's Nullstellensatz MvPolynomial.isMaximal\_iff\_eq\_vanishingIdeal\_singleton and comaps along K\[X\] -\> K\[X\] / I. So both readings are formalised; which wording the editors want is recorded as a question for them, not as an error. (2) 'the fibers of the map Spec O\_F -\> Spec Z, where the fiber above a rational prime p is the set of primes of O\_F lying above p': PrimeSpectrum.preimage\_comap\_singleton\_eq\_primesOver, for any R -\> S the preimage of a point P of Spec R under Spec S -\> Spec R is \{Q \| Q in P.primesOver S\} (Mathlib's Ideal.primesOver, the primes lying over P). NumberField.range\_fiberι\_spec\_map\_algebraMap\_int: for the ring of integers O\_F (any field F : Type) and the point (p) of Spec Z (p a prime number, or p = 0 for the generic point), the underlying set of the scheme-theoretic fibre (Mathlib's AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.fiber, embedded by fiberι, through Scheme.Hom.range\_fiberι) is that set. Review: statements and proofs checked; no statement changed (a module docstring that called the LMFDB's sentence false rewritten; a doubly qualified name replaced by dot notation). lake build through the guard; \#lint (15 linters) clean; axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound (the preimage lemma: propext, Quot.sound); both simp lemmas needed (deletion test); non-vacuity in scratch Probe.lean (the plane curve y\^2 = x\^3 - x over C, the coordinate ring C\[X\] / I(V) of an affine algebraic set V, the points (2) and (0) of Spec Z); the six public names are new in Mathlib, Tau Ceti and LeanBridge.
