* [`nf.reflex_reflex_field`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Fields/Number-fields/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_nf___reflex_reflex_field_FLQQ_--statement) — Reflex field of the reflex field. Declarations (LeanBridge): `NumberField.CMType.reflexReflexField`, `NumberField.CMType.IsInducedFrom`, `NumberField.CMType.induce`, `NumberField.CMType.mem_inverseType_iff_comp_imageFieldConj_notMem`, `NumberField.CMType.map_algebraMap_reflexReflexField_eq_fixedField_inverseTypeStabilizer`, `NumberField.CMType.map_algebraMap_reflexReflexField`, `NumberField.CMType.isLeast_reflexReflexField`, `NumberField.CMType.map_reflexReflexField_eq_reflexField_reflexType`. Note: Round AJ (AJ7). The three gaps of the sweep of 2026-11-06 (that Phi is induced from reflexReflexField, its agreement with the knowl's definition, the stabiliser description) are closed, unconditionally. ReflexReflexFieldGalois: for any Galois extension Omega of Q (finite or not) and j : K -\>+\* Omega, precompStabilizer of the CM type Phi\_Omega = Phi.induce j (the g with chi o g in Phi\_Omega iff chi in Phi\_Omega, which is \{g \| Phi\_Omega o g = Phi\_Omega\} by mem\_precompStabilizer\_iff\_image\_comp\_eq: the stabiliser for the right action by precomposition) contains the open subgroup fixing the normal closure of j(K), so it is closed and equals the group fixing its fixed field; Phi is induced from M iff j(M) contains that fixed field (isInducedFrom\_iff\_fixedField\_le, through isInducedFrom\_iff\_forall\_comp\_subtype\_eq and the transitivity of Gal(Omega/Q) on embeddings). Hence map\_reflexReflexField\_eq\_fixedField (j(reflexReflexField) is that fixed field); isInducedFrom\_reflexReflexField and isLeast\_reflexReflexField (paragraph 3, the smallest field of definition, 'largest' corrected); map\_algebraMap\_reflexReflexField (paragraph 2 as corrected: for N finite Galois over Q containing K, such as a normal closure, the subfield of N fixed by the stabiliser of Phi\_N under the right action of Gal(N/Q) by precomposition is the reflex field of the reflex field); and, for K CM and a complex embedding phi0, stabilizer\_reflexType (the Gal(Qbar/Q)-stabiliser of the reflex type is precompStabilizer of Phi.induce phi0), so map\_reflexReflexField\_eq\_reflexField\_reflexType: phi0(reflexReflexField) = (Phi.reflexType phi0).reflexField, the classical 'reflex field of the reflex type'. ReflexReflexFieldInverseType, paragraph 1 literally: for N finite Galois over Q, imageField N is the image F of N in C (fieldRange\_eq\_imageField: every complex embedding has image F), inverse chi : F -\>+\* N, inverseType (the inverses of the embeddings in a CM type of N) is a CM type on F with values in N (mem\_inverseType\_iff\_comp\_imageFieldConj\_notMem: exactly one of psi and psi o (complex conjugation on F) lies in it), its stabiliser inverseTypeStabilizer = \{g \| g o Psi = Psi\} (mem\_inverseTypeStabilizer\_iff\_image\_comp\_eq) equals precompStabilizer (inverseTypeStabilizer\_eq), so map\_algebraMap\_reflexReflexField\_eq\_fixedField\_inverseTypeStabilizer: the reflex field of this CM type, the subfield of N that this stabiliser fixes, is the image of reflexReflexField. Also linkable if the cap allows: precompStabilizer, inverseType, inverseTypeStabilizer, isInducedFrom\_reflexReflexField, mem\_precompStabilizer\_iff\_image\_comp\_eq. Text: the two recorded corrections (lmfdb-knowl-edits.md: 'largest' -\> 'smallest'; Gal(N/K) acting on the CM types of K -\> Gal(N/Q) acting on the CM types of N by precomposition, stabilising Phi\_N) are fixable texts (ruling of 2026-11-11) and their corrected statements are proved. New pure typo (does not affect the outcome): 'and let \$N\$ a normal closure of \$K\$,' -\> 'and let \$N\$ be a normal closure of \$K\$,'. Stale docstrings in the committed ReflexReflexField.lean (module docstring lines 26-28, reflexReflexField docstring lines 58-60: these facts 'are not proved here') should point to ReflexReflexFieldGalois at the merge. Review (AJ7): for