tion, nilpotency being invariant), and the exception, Group.IsIsoclinic.nilpotencyClass\_ne\_of\_subsingleton (review, Isoclinism/DerivedLength.lean: the class of the trivial group, 0, differs from that of every nontrivial group isoclinic to it). '... and solvable length are (except for the trivial group)': the text links group.derived\_series, whose derived length is the index where the derived series becomes stationary, for every finite group; with it the claim fails for A\_5 and A\_5 x C\_2 (the recorded correction of lmfdb-knowl-edits-zz.md, 'and, for solvable groups, ... solvable length ...', for the editors: a corrected range, fixable under the ruling of 2026-11-11). Proved: for solvable groups, Group.IsIsoclinic.isSolvable\_iff and Group.IsIsoclinic.derivedLength\_eq (nontrivial; the corrected statement); and on the whole range where the uncorrected claim is true, Group.IsIsoclinic.derivedLength\_eq\_of\_isPerfect\_iff (review: isoclinic groups that are both perfect or both not have the same derived length, for every group, so also S\_5 and S\_5 x C\_2), so no true claim is dropped whichever wording the editors choose; the exception, Group.IsIsoclinic.derivedLength\_ne\_of\_subsingleton (review). The recorded reason 'solvable length is an invariant only for solvable groups' (tracker v59 blocker) is imprecise: the derived length fails to be invariant exactly between a perfect group and a non-perfect one. Not linked for want of room (eight links): IsIsoclinic.refl, symm, trans, exists\_isStemGroup\_isIsoclinic, isNilpotent\_iff, isSolvable\_iff, the two exception lemmas, Group.isIsoclinic\_of\_surjective, Group.isIsoclinic\_quotient, Group.Isoclinism.centerInfCommutatorEquiv.
