* [`group.metabelian`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Abstract-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_group___metabelian_FLQQ_--statement) — Metabelian group. Declarations (LeanBridge): `IsMetabelian`, `isMetabelian_iff_exists_normal`, `IsMetacyclic.isMetabelian`, `DihedralGroup.isMetabelian`, `QuaternionGroup.isMetabelian`, `IsExtraspecial.isMetabelian`, `IsPGroup.isMetabelian_of_pRank_le_one`, `not_isMetacyclic_elementaryAbelian_two_three`. Note: Round AJ (AJ7). The last gaps of AD2 ('p-groups of p-rank one are metabelian; p-rank is not defined; no IsExtraspecial definition') are closed, without the classification of these groups as cyclic or generalised quaternion. Group.pRank p G (MetabelianPRankOne) is the largest n such that G has an elementary abelian subgroup of order p\^n (an abelian subgroup all of whose elements satisfy h\^p = 1), the rank the knowl means (not group.rank's minimal number of generators). IsPGroup.isMetabelian\_of\_pRank\_le\_one: a finite p-group of p-rank at most one (in particular of p-rank one) is metabelian. Route: a maximal abelian normal subgroup A of a finite p-group contains its centraliser (IsPGroup.centralizer\_le\_of\_maximal: otherwise the image of C\_G(A) in the nilpotent G/A is a nontrivial normal subgroup, which meets the centre in some xA != 1, and the preimage of \<xA\> is abelian, normal and strictly larger); in a p-group of p-rank \<= 1 every abelian subgroup is cyclic (IsPGroup.isCyclic\_of\_pRank\_le\_one: exponent = order, by induction on the exponent p\^k through the p\^(k-1)-power map, whose image is elementary abelian, so of order \<= p); so A is cyclic, Aut(A) is abelian (IsCyclic.mulAutMulEquiv), every commutator acts trivially on A and lies in C\_G(A) = A (IsPGroup.isMetabelian\_of\_forall\_normal\_isCyclic). Non-vacuity: Group.pRank\_multiplicative\_zmod (C\_p has p-rank one); QuaternionGroup.pRank\_two (every dicyclic group has 2-rank one, its only element of order 2 being a n) with QuaternionGroup.isPGroup\_two\_pow (QuaternionGroup (2\^k), the generalised quaternion groups, are 2-groups). Extraspecial groups (ExtraspecialMetabelian): IsExtraspecial p G (a p-group whose centre has order p and equals both the commutator and the Frattini subgroup), IsExtraspecial.isMetabelian (the commutator subgroup is central), example TauCeti.HeisenbergGroup.isExtraspecial\_zmod (the Heisenberg group over F\_p; through IsPGroup.frattini\_eq\_closure\_sup\_commutator, the Frattini subgroup of a finite p-group is generated by the p-th powers and the commutators, from Tau Ceti's pro-p Frattini description). Every sentence is now proved: the definition, the extension equivalence, solvability and the abelian case (instances in Metabelian.lean), dihedral, quaternion (dicyclic), metacyclic, extraspecial groups and p-groups of p-rank one, and C\_2\^3 metabelian but not metacyclic. Also linkable if the cap allows: the definitions Group.pRank and IsExtraspecial, isMetabelian\_of\_commutator\_le\_center. Text: the recorded correction 'and groups of \$p\$-rank one.' -\> 'and \$p\$-groups of \$p\$-rank one.' (A\_5 has 3-rank one) is a fixable text (ruling of 2026-11-11); the typo 'metacylic' is recorded too. Overlap with Tau Ceti main: main has TauCeti.HeisenbergGroup.commutator\_eq\_zAxis (Heisenberg/Basic.lean), absent at the pin; ExtraspecialMetabelian proves it as a private auxiliary, to be replaced at the bump. Review (AJ7): formalised, confirmed. Group.pRank is the standard p-rank (largest rank of an elementary abelian p-subgroup), the one of the recorded correction; the LMFDB has no group p-rank (its source has only av.fq.p\_rank), and a p-group of rank one in the sense of group.rank is cyclic, so that reading is covered too. IsExtraspecial is the standard definition (Z(P) = P' = Phi(P) of order p; the LMFDB has no group.extraspecial knowl), met by the Heisenberg group over F\_p (D\_4 for p = 2). Every sentence of the knowl has its declaration (table in review/AJ7\_small.md).
