* [`group.monomial`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Abstract-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_group___monomial_FLQQ_--statement) — Monomial group. Declarations (LeanBridge): `IsMGroup`, `IsMGroup.isSolvable`, `IsMGroup.of_isSupersolvable`, `IsMGroup.of_isSolvable_of_isAGroup`, `IsMGroup.of_isSupersolvable_quotient`, `not_forall_isSupersolvable_of_isMGroup`, `not_forall_isSupersolvable_of_isSolvable_of_isAGroup`, `not_forall_isMGroup_of_isSolvable`. Note: Round AJ (AJ2). Every mathematical statement of the knowl is proved for IsMGroup (finite G : Type; every simple W : FDRep ℂ G is isomorphic to Ind\_H\^G of a linear character χ : H →\* ℂˣ). (1) 'Such a group is always solvable': Taketa's theorem IsMGroup.isSolvable (Isaacs, Character Theory, 5.12): by induction on n the n-th derived subgroup acts trivially on every irreducible representation of degree at most n; for W ≅ Ind\_H\^G χ of degree n + 1 = \[G : H\], the augmentation subrepresentation of ℂ\[G/H\] (Tau Ceti) has degree n, so G⁽ⁿ⁾ fixes every coset and lies in H, and G⁽ⁿ⁺¹⁾ ≤ \[H, H\] ≤ ker χ together with its conjugates. (2) 'monomial groups include all supersolvable groups and solvable A-groups': IsMGroup.of\_isSupersolvable (Huppert) and IsMGroup.of\_isSolvable\_of\_isAGroup (Isaacs 6.23), both cases of IsMGroup.of\_isSupersolvable\_quotient (Isaacs 6.22: a normal solvable A-subgroup N with G/N supersolvable). The proof extends Tau Ceti's nilpotent case (FDRep.exists\_character\_eq\_indClassFun\_of\_isNilpotent): for W not induced from a proper subgroup, every normal subgroup acting through commuting operators acts centrally (Clifford correspondence at the inertia group, Tau Ceti's exists\_simple\_liesOver\_inertia\_nonempty\_iso\_indFDRep and commute\_of\_inertia\_eq\_top); going up the derived series of N each term acts through a quotient that is nilpotent of class at most 2 and an A-group, hence abelian (IsAGroup.commutatorElement\_mem\_of\_forall\_commutatorElement\_mem); and a proper centrally acting Z with G/Z supersolvable would give x ∉ Z with ⟨x⟩Z normal and acting through commuting operators. No extension of characters is needed. (3) The three non-implications, on LMFDB groups: A₄ is a solvable A-group (cube-free order 12, IsAGroup.of\_forall\_not\_pow\_three\_dvd\_card), hence monomial (alternatingGroup.isMGroup\_fin\_four), but not supersolvable (alternatingGroup.not\_isSupersolvable\_fin\_four, by decide +kernel: no nontrivial cyclic normal subgroup): not\_forall\_isSupersolvable\_of\_isMGroup and not\_forall\_isSupersolvable\_of\_isSolvable\_of\_isAGroup; SL(2, 3) is solvable (Burnside's pᵃqᵇ theorem, Tau Ceti) but not monomial (Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.not\_isMGroup\_fin\_two\_zmod\_three: 7 conjugacy classes, from the 168 commuting pairs, so the squares of the seven irreducible degrees sum to 24 and one degree is 2; SL(2, 3) is generated by squares, so it has no subgroup of index 2; and in an M-group every irreducible degree is the index of a subgroup, IsMGroup.exists\_index\_eq\_characterDegree): not\_forall\_isMGroup\_of\_isSolvable. 'A purely group-theoretic description of monomial groups is not known' is a remark on the literature, not a mathematical statement. Axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound only (the finite checks use decide +kernel).
* [`group.name`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Abstract-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_group___name_FLQQ_--statement) — Abstract group name. Declarations (Tau Ceti · LeanBridge): `TauCeti.AffineGroup`, `TauCeti.AffineGroup.mulEquivRangeToPermHom`, `OtherDihedralGroup`, `ZMod.involutionMulAut_otherDihedralUnit_ne_one`, `SemidirectProduct.nonempty_mulEquiv_otherDihedralGroup_iff`, `TauCeti.HeisenbergGroup.natCard_zmod`, `TauCeti.HeisenbergGroup.exponent_zmod`, `TauCeti.HeisenbergGroup.nonempty_mulEquiv_of_exponent_eq`. Note: Round AI (AI1), from the Nothing-to-formalise audit (N2: Partially in LeanBridge, easy); formalised with a range correction (fixable text, ruling of 2026-11-11), confirmed in review. The knowl is mostly notation (C\_n, S\_n, A\_n, D\_n of order 2n, Q\_n, SD\_n and OD\_n of order n = 2\^k, the sporadic and Lie-type names, A x B, A:B with A normal, A.B, A wr B), each building block having its own knowl; Mathlib's and LeanBridge's conventions agree with it (DihedralGroup.nat\_card, QuaternionGroup.card, SemiDihedralGroup.card, OtherDihedralGroup.card). It states three facts. (1) F\_q: 'the group of affine linear transformations of F\_q ... a semidirect product F\_q : F\_q\^x': Tau Ceti's AffineGroup F is by definition Multiplicative F x\|\[affineAction F\] F\^x, and LeanBridge's TauCeti.AffineGroup.mulEquivRangeToPermHom (with mem\_range\_toPermHom\_iff) identifies it with the group of the maps x -\> a x + b, a != 0 (as for group.frobenius). (2) He\_p, 'the unique non-abelian group of order p\^3 and exponent p for an odd prime p': natCard\_zmod (order p\^3), TauCeti.HeisenbergGroup.not\_isMulCommutative (non-abelian; not linked for want of room), exponent\_zmod (exponent p for p odd) and nonempty\_mulEquiv\_of\_exponent\_eq (uniqueness), all from round AG5. (3) OD\_n, 'the non-trivial semidirect product C\_\{2\^\{k-1\}\} : C\_2 which is not isomorphic to either SD\_n or D\_\{2\^\{k-1\}\}': SemidirectProduct.nonempty\_mulEquiv\_otherDihedralGroup\_iff: for k \>= 4, any cyclic N of order 2\^(k-1), any H of order 2 and any non-trivial phi : H -\>\* MulAut N, N x\|\[phi\] H is isomorphic to OD\_\{2\^k\} iff it is isomorphic to neither SD\_\{2\^k\} nor D\_\{2\^\{k-1\}\}; and OD\_\{2\^k\} is itself such a product (OtherDihedralGroup is the semidirect product for involutionMulAut of the unit 2\^(k-2)+1, non-trivial by ZMod.involutionMulAut\_otherDihedralUnit\_ne\_one), so it is the one the sentence names, up to isomorphism. 'Non-trivial' is read as phi != 1, which is the same as the product not being the direct product (SemidirectProduct.not\_isMulCommutative\_of\_ne\_one). Proof: N x\|\[phi\] H has order 2\^k, the image of N is cyclic of index 2, and it is non-abelian; round AF's classification nonempty\_mulEquiv\_of\_isCyclic\_of\_index\_eq\_two leaves D, Q, SD, OD; Q is excluded because g\^2 = 1 has 2 solutions in Q\_\{2\^k\} (QuaternionGroup.card\_sq\_eq\_one) and at least 3 in the product (1, an involution of N by Cauchy, the generator of H); the converse uses DihedralGroup.isEmpty\_mulEquiv\_otherDihedralGroup and SemiDihedralGroup.isEmpty\_mulEquiv\_otherDihedralGroup. Non-vacuity re-checked in scratch (N = C\_\{2\^\{k-1\}\}, H = C\_2 with OD's own action and with SD's). Text error (changes the mathematics, fixable): for k = 3 the description fails, since OD\_8 is D\_4, now proved (added in review): OtherDihedralGroup.nonempty\_mulEquiv\_dihedralGroup : Nonempty (OtherDihedralGroup 3 ≃\* DihedralGroup 4) (the unit 2\^(3-2)+1 = 3 is -1 in ZMod 4). Old: 'of order \$n=2\^k\$. It is the non-trivial' (occurs once in the live text and in the blueprint copy). New: 'of order \$n=2\^k\$ with \$k \\geq 4\$. It is the non-trivial'. The LMFDB's search accepts OD\_n for any power of 2 (lmfdb/groups/abstract/main.py, valid\_params, checked), so the range belongs in the text. Checks re-run: lake build through the guard; \#lint in the module (15 linters, 0 errors on 6 declarations); \#print axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound (not\_isMulCommutative\_of\_ne\_one: propext, Quot.sound); names new in the three trees and on Tau Ceti main (the index helper is private, as OtherDihedralGroup.index\_range\_inl and SemiDihedralGroup.index\_range\_inl exist: fold item); simp deletion test (the three entries of the two lists are needed).
* [`group.nilpotent`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Abstract-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_group___nilpotent_FLQQ_--statement) — Nilpotent group. Declarations (Mathlib · LeanBridge): `Group.IsNilpotent`, `Group.nilpotencyClass`, `Group.isNilpotent_of_finite_tfae`, `Subgroup.least_ascending_central_series_length_eq_nilpotencyClass`, `Group.IsNilpotent.isSupersolvable`, `Group.not_forall_isNilpotent_of_isNilpotent_quotient`. Note: Proved the two missing facts. Group.IsNilpotent.isSupersolvable: a finite nilpotent group is supersolvable in LeanBridge's sense (Group.IsSupersolvable, a normal series with cyclic factors and all terms normal in G), by adjoining at each step an element whose image in G ⧸ Nᵢ is a nontrivial central element (the centre of a nontrivial nilpotent group is nontrivial). Not closed under extensions, stated as such (review): Group.not\_forall\_isNilpotent\_of\_isNilpotent\_quotient, from DihedralGroup.not\_isNilpotent (Dₙ, odd n ≠ 1, e.g. D₃ ≅ S₃, has trivial centre) with DihedralGroup.isNilpotent\_dihedralRotations and DihedralGroup.isNilpotent\_quotient\_dihedralRotations (its normal rotation subgroup Cₙ, Tau Ceti's dihedralRotations, and the quotient C₂ are nilpotent). The rest is covered as the sweep found: the finite characterisations and central series (Mathlib), solvability, closure under subgroups and quotients (Mathlib), monomiality (LeanBridge's IsMGroup.of\_isNilpotent); the optional -1 convention is not a claim. The knowl's 'supersolvable' is about finite groups, the knowl's context (an infinite abelian group such as ℚ is nilpotent but not supersolvable).
