* [`group.orthogonal`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Abstract-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_group___orthogonal_FLQQ_--statement) — Orthogonal group. Declarations (Tau Ceti · LeanBridge): `TauCeti.QuadraticMap.orthogonalGroup`, `TauCeti.QuadraticMap.specialOrthogonalGroup`, `QuadraticForm.projectiveOrthogonalGroup`, `QuadraticForm.projectiveSpecialOrthogonalGroup`, `QuadraticForm.ellipticForm`, `QuadraticForm.exists_equivalent_smul_parabolicForm`, `QuadraticForm.equivalent_hyperbolicForm_or_equivalent_ellipticForm`, `QuadraticForm.not_equivalent_smul_hyperbolicForm_ellipticForm`. Note: Round AG (AG5). Formalised, with the recorded corrections (fixable text, ruling of 2026-11-11): the classes are those of nondegenerate forms (Mathlib's QuadraticMap.Nondegenerate, valid in every characteristic; the proofs only use a trivial radical), and the knowl's 'one equivalence class' in odd dimension is read as one similarity class. The recorded parenthesis 'for q odd there are two isometry classes, which differ by a scalar factor' is now proved too: for odd q and a non-square nu every nondegenerate form of dimension 2m+1 is isometric to the parabolic form P or to nu . P (equivalent\_parabolicForm\_or\_equivalent\_smul\_parabolicForm), and P, nu . P are not isometric, since they take the value 1 a different number of times, 2A + (q - 2)B against qB with A != B the numbers of zeros and of solutions of H = 1 for the hyperbolic part (not\_equivalent\_smul\_parabolicForm). The blocker, the classification of nondegenerate quadratic forms over finite fields, is proved for every finite field F, both parities of q: odd dimension 2m+1, every nondegenerate Q has c . Q isometric to the parabolic form z\^2 + x1 y1 + ... + xm ym for a unit c (exists\_equivalent\_smul\_parabolicForm); even dimension 2m+2, every nondegenerate Q is isometric to the hyperbolic form (+) or to the elliptic form (-) (equivalent\_hyperbolicForm\_or\_equivalent\_ellipticForm), and no scalar multiple