alGroupEquivOfSMul (still named in the module docstring). The counts are exact, each class containing a nondegenerate form: the standard forms are nondegenerate in every characteristic (committed OmegaGroup.lean: nondegenerate\_parabolicForm', nondegenerate\_hyperbolicForm', nondegenerate\_ellipticForm), and, added in review, so is c . P for every unit c (nondegenerate\_smul\_parabolicForm, from Tau Ceti's QuadraticMap.nondegenerate\_smul\_iff), which the parenthesis needs for nu . P. Nondegenerate is Mathlib's QuadraticMap.Nondegenerate (the quadratic radical \{Q v = 0, polar Q v = 0\} is trivial and the polar kernel has rank at most 1), the right notion in characteristic 2. Range confirmed: the LMFDB's orthogonal-group names come from Magma's constructors (gps\_families.magma\_cmd), defined for n odd \>= 3 (GO, SO, Omega) and n even \>= 2 (+ and - types), so n = 0 is outside its setting; the theorems cover every n \>= 1. Transfer checked: O(c . Q) = O(Q), and conjugation by the isometry e from c . Q to Q' (Tau Ceti's orthogonalGroupCongr, specialOrthogonalGroupCongr) carries scalars to scalars, so PGO and PSO follow (quotientScalarSubgroupEquiv). Review changes are style only besides the new lemma: binders hoisted, packing, deletion test (47 simp entries and 5 calls dropped).
