on of the 2-chains onto the 2-cycles; finiteness by Schur's theorem). Closes the tracker v60c blocker except its last item 'and H\_2(G, Z) = H\^2(G, C\^x)', which no sentence of the knowl states: TauCeti.schurMultiplier (H\^2(G, k\^x), Tau Ceti's cohomological model), linked in the 11-06 record, is dropped from the decls, as it is not the knowl's object and its comparison with H\_2(G, Z) (H\^2(G, C\^x) = Hom(H\_2(G, Z), C\^x) = H\_2(G, Z) for finite G) is not proved; the pairing of CentralExtension.lean is one half of it. If the blueprint keeps it as related material it should say so. Checks: lake build of the four modules, \#lint 0 errors, axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. Lean: 1048 new lines in four files, shared with group.stem\_extension. Also linkable: nat\_card\_H2\_kleinFour (an example the knowl does not state), GroupExtension.IsStem.H2ToKernel, SchurCover.extension, MonoidHom.surjective\_H2ToKerInfCommutator, MonoidHom.mem\_range\_H2ToCenter\_iff. Review (AM5\_schur review, 2026-11-17): formalised, confirmed. H2 (Rep.trivial Z G Z) is Mathlib's groupHomology (Rep.trivial Z G Z) 2 itself (an abbrev); every claim is proved for the LMFDB's finite groups, none through a junk value (C and K are finite). Links: GroupExtension.IsStem.nat\_card\_kernel\_le (\|K\| \<= \|H\_2(G, Z)\|, the literal 'maximal' by size; made a theorem with a docstring) replaces nat\_card\_H2\_kleinFour; dropping TauCeti.schurMultiplier is right (it is H\^2(G, k\^x) for any commutative semiring k, e.g. H\^2(C\_2, R\^x) = C\_2 while H\_2(C\_2, Z) = 0, and not a DEFINES link). The data sentence is a storage convention (the LMFDB's schur\_multiplier column, displayed by web\_groups.py schur\_multiplier\_text); its premise, a finite abelian group, is SchurCover.finite\_H2. The review changed style, proofs and docstrings, no linked statement (review/AM5\_schur.md).
