ond the eight links: SemiDihedralGroup.isCyclic\_range\_inl, SemiDihedralGroup.card, DihedralGroup.isEmpty\_mulEquiv\_quaternionGroup, DihedralGroup.isEmpty\_mulEquiv\_otherDihedralGroup, QuaternionGroup.isEmpty\_mulEquiv\_otherDihedralGroup, QuaternionGroup.not\_isMulCommutative, OtherDihedralGroup.not\_isMulCommutative/isCyclic\_range\_inl/index\_range\_inl. Review: the helpers take the cyclic subgroup as zpowers a instead of N with N = zpowers a (house rule on x = t hypotheses), and the main proof obtains the generator through Mathlib's Subgroup.isCyclic\_iff\_exists\_zpowers\_eq\_top; statements of the linked theorems unchanged. The same file closes group.other\_dihedral (record below).
