* [`group.stem_extension`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Abstract-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_group___stem_extension_FLQQ_--statement) — Stem extension. Declarations (LeanBridge): `GroupExtension.IsStem`, `Subgroup.IsStem`, `GroupExtension.IsStem.nat_card_le`, `GroupExtension.IsMaximalStem`, `GroupExtension.IsMaximalStem.bijective_H2ToKernel`, `GroupExtension.IsMaximalStem.isIsoclinic`, `GroupExtension.not_forall_nonempty_mulEquiv_of_isMaximalStem`, `GroupExtension.IsMaximalStem.nonempty_mulEquiv`. Note: Round AM (AM5\_schur). Every sentence is proved, for finite G (the LMFDB's abstract groups; G : Type, as Mathlib's groupHomology over Z requires; K and C in any universe). Closes the whole tracker v60c blocker ('Schur's theory of stem extensions of a finite group G (\|K\| \<= \|M(G)\|, so \|C\| is bounded; K = M(G) when \|C\| is maximal; Schur covers unique up to isoclinism, and up to isomorphism for perfect G)'), with M(G) = H\_2(G, Z) = groupHomology (Rep.trivial Z G Z) 2, the definition of group.schur\_multiplier. Nothing from Tau Ceti's main is used (its MonoidHom.CentralCover, universal central extensions of perfect groups, has no link to H\_2(G, Z) and is not needed). Definition: the committed GroupExtension.IsStem and Subgroup.IsStem (K \<= Z(C) cap C'). Text error already recorded, fixable (lmfdb-knowl-edits.md, section group.stem\_extension): Old '\{\{KNOWL('group.commutator\_subgroup', 'commutator')\}\} of \$G\$' New '\{\{KNOWL('group.commutator\_subgroup', 'commutator')\}\} of \$C\$' (the center too is that of C). Route. (1) CentralExtension.lean, for any group G: for pi : C -\>\* G with central kernel N and a section sigma, the factor set alpha(g, h) = sigma(g) sigma(h) sigma(gh)\^-1 in Z(C) (MonoidHom.centralFactorSet) pairs with the inhomogeneous 2-chains of the trivial representation Z of G and kills the boundaries (cocycle identity), giving theta : H\_2(G, Z) -\> Z(C) (MonoidHom.H2ToCenter). Its image is exactly N cap C' (MonoidHom.mem\_range\_H2ToCenter\_iff): it lies in C' because the image of a cycle in C\^ab is that of its boundary under \[g\] -\> sigma(g) C'; conversely, if z in N cap C' were not in the image, a Q/Z-valued character chi of Z(C) killing the image but not z (Mathlib's CharacterModule) makes chi o alpha vanish on the 2-cycles, so it factors through the boundary map and extends to the 1-chains (Q/Z injective, CharacterModule.dual\_surjective\_of\_injective): chi(alpha(g, h)) = b(g) + b(h) - b(gh); then c -\> chi(c sigma(pi c)\^-1) + b(pi c) is a homomorphism C -\> Q/Z extending chi, which kills C', so chi(z) = 0, a contradiction. Hence N cap C' is a quotient of H\_2(G, Z) (MonoidHom.surjective\_H2ToKerInfCommutator). (2) SchurCover.lean: the 1-boundaries are a free Z-module (Tau Ceti's Submodule.free\_of\_isPrincipalIdealRing, any rank), so the 2-cycles are a retract of the 2-chains; extending Z\_2 -\> H\_2 gives a normalised 2-cocycle with values in H\_2(G, Z) (SchurCover.factorSet, a Tau Ceti FactorSet for the trivial action) whose extension SchurCover G has theta = the inclusion of H\_2(G, Z), so SchurCover.extension : 1 -\> H\_2(G, Z) -\> SchurCover G -\> G -\> 1 is a stem extension (SchurCover.isStem\_extension, any G). For finite G its centre has finite index, so its commutator subgroup is finite by Schur's theorem (Mathlib's instance for finitely many commutators; the commutator set is finite through Group.centralCommutatorMap) and H\_2(G, Z) is finite (SchurCover.finite\_H2). (3) MaximalStem.lean. 'For fixed G, the size of C is bounded': GroupExtension.IsStem.nat\_card\_le, \|C\| \<= \|G\| \|H\_2(G, Z)\| for every stem extension, C being finite (GroupExtension.IsStem.finite, so no junk value), the bound attained by the Schur cover (SchurCover.nat\_card). 'For any extension with C of maximal size, the kernel K is isomorphic to the Schur multiplier': GroupExtension.IsMaximalStem (a stem extension with \|C'\| \<= \|C\| for every stem extension 1 -\> K' -\> C' -\> G -\> 1, K', C' : Type), equivalent to \|K\| = \|H\_2(G, Z)\| (GroupExtension.isMaximalStem\_iff); then the homomorphism H\_2(G, Z) -\> K of GroupExtension.IsStem.H2ToKernel is bijective (GroupExtension.IsMaximalStem.bijective\_H2ToKernel); maximal ones exist (SchurCover.isMaximalStem\_extension). 'In general, C is only determined up to isoclinism in such an extension': GroupExtension.IsMaximalStem.isIsoclinic (the fibre product P of C\_1 and C\_2 over G is a central extension of G, \|ker cap P'\| \<= \|H\_2(G, Z)\| = \|K\_1\| by MonoidHom.nat\_card\_ker\_inf\_commutator\_le, and the first projection maps ker cap P' onto K\_1 \<= C\_1', so the kernel of P -\> C\_1 meets P' trivially and round AL's Group.isIsoclinic\_of\_surjective applies; likewise for C\_2), and the 'only': GroupExtension.not\_forall\_nonempty\_mulEquiv\_of\_isMaximalStem (KleinFour.lean: D\_4 and Q\_8 are the middle groups of stem extensions of maximal size of C\_2 x C\_2, DihedralGroup.isMaximalStem\_reduceModTwoExtension and QuaternionGroup.isMaximalStem\_reduceModTwoExtension, not isomorphic by the committed DihedralGroup.isEmpty\_mulEquiv\_quaternionGroup; maximality from \|H\_2(C\_2 x C\_2, Z)\| = 2, nat\_card\_H2\_kleinFour, whose upper bound is MonoidHom.nat\_card\_ker\_le\_two: the kernel of a stem extension of C\_2 x C\_2 is C' \<= \<\[x, y\]\> with \[x, y\]\^2 = \[x\^2, y\] = 1, applied to the Schur cover). 'but if G is perfect then C is determined up to isomorphism': GroupExtension.IsMaximalStem.nonempty\_mulEquiv (C\_1 and C\_2 are perfect, GroupExtension.IsStem.isPerfect, and both projections map P' isomorphically onto them). Checks: lake build of the four modules, \#lint 0 errors, axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound, every multi-lemma simp list checked by single deletion, no name clash in the three trees or Tau Ceti main. Lean: 1048 new lines in four files (CentralExtension 238, SchurCover 236, MaximalStem 333, KleinFour 241). Also linkable: GroupExtension.IsStem.finite, GroupExtension.isMaximalStem\_iff, SchurCover.isMaximalStem\_extension, SchurCover.nat\_card, GroupExtension.IsStem.isPerfect, DihedralGroup.isMaximalStem\_reduceModTwoExtension, QuaternionGroup.isMaximalStem\_reduceModTwoExtension, MonoidHom.nat\_card\_ker\_inf\_commutator\_le. Review (AM5\_schur review, 2026-11-17): formalised, confirmed, links unchanged. IsMaximalStem is the knowl's 'C of maximal size' among the stem extensions of G; it compares only the stem extensions with K', C' : Type, which loses nothing for finite G (a maximal one bounds the stem extensions in every universe, and maximality among those of any one universe implies IsMaximalStem: both checked in the review's Probe.lean; the docstring now says so). The fibre-product proof of isIsoclinic uses both maximality hypotheses and round AL's isIsoclinic\_of\_surjective; the D\_4 / Q\_8 non-uniqueness quantifies over finite G and is witnessed by finite groups; nonempty\_mulEquiv is non-vacuous (SL(2, 5) with its Schur cover). The review changed style, proofs and docstrings, no linked statement: the helper MonoidHom.ker\_inf\_commutator\_eq\_bot has its equation hypothesis substituted, and GroupExtension.bijective\_comp\_subtype\_commutator is now proved from round AL's Group.bijective\_codRestrict\_domRestrict\_commutator; the review's deletion test found three deletable simp entries and an unused have (removed); dup\_decls 0 clashes (review/AM5\_schur.md).
* [`group.stem_group`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Abstract-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_group___stem_group_FLQQ_--statement) — Stem group. Declarations (LeanBridge): `Group.IsStemGroup`, `Group.exists_isStemGroup_isIsoclinic`, `Group.exists_finite_isStemGroup_isIsoclinic`, `Group.not_forall_nonempty_mulEquiv_of_isStemGroup`, `Group.isIsoclinic_dihedralGroup_quaternionGroup`, `Group.IsStemGroup.nat_card_dvd`, `Group.IsStemGroup.finite_of_isIsoclinic`, `Group.IsStemGroup.lift_mk_dvd`. Note: Round AL (AL3\_stem\_groups), reviewed (review/AL3\_stem\_groups.md). Every sentence is proved; the blocker of tracker v59 and the quote of the 11-06 sweep ('Any group is isoclinic to a stem group (not necessarily unique), and the order of a stem group divides the order of every other group in its isoclinism class') are closed. Definition: Group.IsStemGroup (Z(G) \<= G', StemExtension.lean). 'Any group is isoclinic to a stem group': Group.exists\_isStemGroup\_isIsoclinic, P. Hall's theorem for every group G : Type u, the stem group in the same universe, and Group.exists\_finite\_isStemGroup\_isIsoclinic, a finite group is isoclinic to a finite stem group (the LMFDB's setting). Route: a surjection f : G -\> H with ker f cap G' = 1 is an isoclinism (Group.Isoclinism.ofSurjective: f\^-1(Z(H)) = Z(G) by comap\_center\_eq\_of\_surjective, and f maps G' isomorphically onto H'), so G is isoclinic to G/N when N cap G' = 1 (isIsoclinic\_quotient); the fibre product P = abelianizationPullback G \<= G x Z\[G\] of G -\> G\^ab and eps : Z\[G\] -\> G\^ab, \[g\] -\> g G' (Z\[G\] = FreeAbelianGroup G) is isoclinic to G by its first projection (surjective, kernel meeting P' = G' x 0 trivially); the second projection embeds Z(P)/(Z(P) cap P') in Z\[G\] (a central (g, 0) has g in G' and is the commutator element of P over g), so that quotient is a free Z-module (Tau Ceti's Module.Free.of\_injective\_of\_projective\_of\_isPrincipalIdealRing, any rank, at the pin; the same statement on main) and Z(P) cap P' has a complement T in Z(P) (exists\_complement\_center\_inf\_commutator, a section of the projective quotient); P/T is a stem group (isStemGroup\_quotient: Z(P/T) is the image of Z(P) \<= T P') isoclinic to P (T cap P' = 1). No minimal-order argument (round ZZ's record: it cannot reach a stem group). '(not necessarily unique)': Group.not\_forall\_nonempty\_mulEquiv\_of\_isStemGroup, restricted by the review to finite groups (the LMFDB's setting; without \[Finite\] it could be witnessed by infinite groups, as for round AJ's non-implications): D\_4 = DihedralGroup 4 and Q\_8 = QuaternionGroup 2 are stem groups (DihedralGroup.isStemGroup\_four from Mathlib's center\_eq\_closure\_of\_even\_ne\_two and r 2 = \[r 1, sr 0\]; QuaternionGroup.isStemGroup\_two, centre \{1, a 2\} by decide and a 2 = \[a 1, xa 0\]), isoclinic (Group.isIsoclinic\_dihedralGroup\_quaternionGroup: both are isoclinic by Isoclinism.ofSurjective to the fibre product of their maps onto C\_2 x C\_2, whose commutators are 1 and (r 2, a 2), a 4096-case kernel decide) and not isomorphic (the committed DihedralGroup.isEmpty\_mulEquiv\_quaternionGroup at k = 3, unchanged by the fold c512b7da). 'the order of a stem group divides the order of every other group in its isoclinism class': Group.IsStemGroup.nat\_card\_dvd (an isoclinism maps Z(G) cap G' onto Z(H) cap H', Group.Isoclinism.centerInfCommutatorEquiv, so \|S\| = \|S/Z(S)\| \|Z(S) cap S'\| divides \|H\| = \|H/Z(H)\| \|Z(H)\|). Not through a junk value in the LMFDB's finite setting: a stem group isoclinic to a finite group is finite (Group.IsStemGroup.finite\_of\_isIsoclinic, which uses the divisibility with \|H\| \> 0), and for groups of every cardinality the divisibility holds in cardinal arithmetic (Group.IsStemGroup.lift\_mk\_dvd). Also proved: isoclinic stem groups have equal orders (IsStemGroup.nat\_card\_eq) and the stem groups of a finite class are its groups of least order (IsStemGroup.isStemGroup\_iff\_nat\_card\_eq). Text: no error. Checks (review): lake build of the four modules, \#lint 0 errors, axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound, every simp list minimal, dup\_decls 0 clashes. Also linkable: Group.IsStemGroup.isStemGroup\_iff\_nat\_card\_eq, DihedralGroup.isStemGroup\_four, QuaternionGroup.isStemGroup\_two, Group.Isoclinism.centerInfCommutatorEquiv.
