* [`group.subgroup.diagram.lmfdb`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Abstract-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_group___subgroup___diagram___lmfdb_FLQQ_--statement) — Subgroup diagrams in the LMFDB. Declarations (Mathlib · LeanBridge · Tau Ceti): `SimpleGraph.hasse`, `CovBy`, `Subgroup.conjClassesDiagram`, `Subgroup.mk_le_mk_iff_exists_smul_le`, `TauCeti.mem_orbit_conjAct_iff`, `Subgroup.index_normalizer_eq_ncard_orbit`, `Subgroup.normal_iff_ncard_orbit_le_one`. Note: Round AI (AI1), from the Nothing-to-formalise audit (N2: Partially in Mathlib, easy); formalised, confirmed in review after one fix. The included group.subgroup.diagram is the Hasse diagram of the subgroups (SimpleGraph.hasse, CovBy; its 'drawn at the same height' is display). The LMFDB's diagram, 'the Hasse diagram on the set of conjugacy classes of subgroups ordered by inclusion': the conjugacy classes of subgroups are MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient (ConjAct G) (Subgroup G), as in Tau Ceti and LeanBridge's ArithmeticallyEquivalent.lean (TauCeti.mem\_orbit\_conjAct\_iff: the orbit of H is its conjugates), and Subgroup.conjClassesDiagram G := SimpleGraph.hasse of it (adjacency = covering, Mathlib's hasse\_adj). Review fix (instance diamond): the author put its own unnamed global Preorder instance on orbitRel.Quotient A (Subgroup G); but Mathlib already has global instances LE (Quotient s) and Preorder (Quotient s) for every setoid on a type with an order (Mathlib.Order.Quotient: Quotient.instLE\_mathlib, Quotient.instPreorder, the transitive closure of 'x \<= y or x \~ y'), orbitRel.Quotient is an abbrev for Quotient, and that module is in the import closure of LeanBridge.lean and of the blueprint Prelude (through TopSlopeRamification.lean and Tau Ceti's ConvexSubgroup), though not of this cluster's modules, so each module built alone. Once both were imported, '\<=' on classes resolved to Mathlib's LE while Preorder resolved to the author's instance, two relations that agree but not definitionally (checked in scratch: Iff.rfl fails). Now the order IS Mathlib's quotient preorder, the order induced by inclusion, and what was a definition is a theorem: Subgroup.mk\_le\_mk\_iff\_exists\_smul\_le: \[H\] \<= \[K\] iff a . H \<= K for some a (a conjugate of H lies in K), for any group A acting on G by automorphisms, so that A = ConjAct G gives conjugacy and A = MulAut G automorphisms (used by group.computing\_subgroup\_labels); Subgroup.mk\_lt\_mk\_iff\_exists\_smul\_le for '\<'. The one instance left is the unnamed PartialOrder for finite G (antisymmetry by counting: a . H \<= K and b . K \<= H force a . H = K), which extends Mathlib's Preorder by rfl (checked with Mathlib.Order.Quotient imported; no other order instance on a quotient exists in Mathlib, Tau Ceti pin or main, or LeanBridge; Mathlib's Quotient.instLinearOrder needs a linear order on Subgroup G); it carries @\[nolint defsWithUnderscore\] as four committed files do (Lean suffixes the generated name: Subgroup.instPartialOrderQuotientOfFinite\_leanBridge). 'The number of subgroups in each conjugacy class is given as a left subscript if it is bigger then one. Hence, normal subgroups are those which have no left subscripts': the number is the size of the orbit, Tau Ceti's Subgroup.index\_normalizer\_eq\_ncard\_orbit (\[G : N\_G(H)\]); Subgroup.normal\_iff\_ncard\_orbit\_le\_one: in a finite group, H is normal iff its class has at most one element (no subscript), from Mathlib's normalizer\_eq\_top\_iff and index\_eq\_one. Dragging, clicking and highlighting are display. Text: 'bigger then one' is a pure typo. Checks re-run on the final file: lake build through the guard; \#lint in the module (15 linters, 0 errors on 6 declarations); \#print axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound; names new in the three trees and on Tau Ceti main; no lemma lists.
