* [`gg.galois_group`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Galois-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_gg___galois_group_FLQQ_--statement) — Galois group. Declarations (Mathlib · Tau Ceti · LeanBridge): `Polynomial.Gal`, `Polynomial.Gal.galActionHom_injective`, `Polynomial.card_rootSet_eq_natDegree`, `Polynomial.Gal.galAction_isPretransitive`, `Equiv.map_permCongrHom_eq_map_conj`, `Subgroup.exists_galActionHom_range_eq_fin`. Note: The converse is proved: for a transitive G \<= Sym(X), X finite and nonempty (and for G \<= S\_n, n \>= 1), there are a field K and an irreducible separable polynomial f over K of degree \|X\| with a labelling e of its roots in its splitting field by X such that the image of Polynomial.Gal f in Sym(roots), transported by e, is exactly G. K is the fixed field of G acting on L = Q(x\_i) by renaming, f = minpoly K x\_\{i0\}; its roots in L are the Galois conjugates g x\_\{i0\} = x\_\{g i0\}, all the x\_i by transitivity; every automorphism of L/K is some g (Artin), acting as x\_i -\> x\_\{g i\}, and Gal.restrict is onto Gal(f); the result is moved to the splitting field through the Galois-equivariant rootsEquivRoots (the general statement for a finite nonempty X is Subgroup.exists\_galActionHom\_range\_eq, in the same file). The rest of the knowl is at the pins: the embedding (galActionHom\_injective, with card\_rootSet\_eq\_natDegree for the n roots), transitivity (galAction\_isPretransitive) and conjugacy of the images under relabelling (Tau Ceti's Equiv.map\_permCongrHom\_eq\_map\_conj). Review: decls now list card\_rootSet\_eq\_natDegree (the n roots of 'embedded in S\_n') instead of the general converse.
