* [`lfunction.history.hecke_operators`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/L-functions/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_lfunction___history___hecke_operators_FLQQ_--statement) — Hecke operators, history. Declarations (Tau Ceti · LeanBridge): `HeckeRing.GL2.Eigenform`, `HeckeRing.GL2.heckeTNat`, `HeckeRing.GL2.Eigenform.qExpansion_coeff_mul`, `HeckeRing.GL2.Eigenform.LSeries_eulerProduct_hasProd`, `CuspForm.frickeCompletedL_eq_mul_LSeries`, `CuspForm.frickeCompletedL_functional_equation_gamma1`, `CuspForm.frickeCompletedL_sub_eq_of_level_one`, `HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.analyticCompletedL_eq_rootNumber_mul`. Note: Round AI (AI5\_mf\_history), reviewed (review/AI5\_mf\_history.md). Audit record N3.json: 'Partially in Tau Ceti', easy, the sentence being an unstated composite. The one mathematical sentence is 'The forms which were simultaneous eigenvalues of these operators have multiplicative Fourier coefficients so that their associated Dirichlet series have Euler products and functional equations.' The rest is history: Hecke and Mordell introduced the operators (Tau Ceti's heckeTNat on M\_k(Gamma\_1(N))), Hecke mainly worked in level 1, and the Atkin-Lehner-Li theory is only named. TEXT ERROR, fixable (ruling of 2026-11-11): 'eigenvalues' is a slip for 'eigenforms', and without 'normalized' the coefficients are not multiplicative (2 Delta: a\_2 a\_3 = -24192, a\_6 = -12096). Old: 'The forms which were simultaneous eigenvalues'; new: 'The normalized forms which were simultaneous eigenforms' (the old string occurs once in the live text). READING (ruling of 2026-11-12, the LMFDB's setting): the forms are cusp forms, at every level. The eigenforms are Tau Ceti's HeckeRing.GL2.Eigenform N k: nonzero cusp forms on Gamma\_1(N) with a nebentypus that are eigenforms of every T\_n, n \>= 1 (every newform is one, Newform.toEigenform). The Eisenstein series, the non-cuspidal eigenforms of level 1, are not covered: no tree proves that they are Hecke eigenforms. Sentence by sentence, for