* [`mf.maass.picard`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Maass-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_mf___maass___picard_FLQQ_--statement) — Maass forms on PSL(2,Z\[i\]). Declarations (LeanBridge): `HyperbolicThreeSpace.PicardGroup`, `HyperbolicThreeSpace.IsPicardMaassForm`, `HyperbolicThreeSpace.picardToPSL_injective`, `HyperbolicThreeSpace.pslEquivOrientationPreservingIsom`, `HyperbolicThreeSpace.toQuaternion_smul`, `HyperbolicThreeSpace.discreteTopology_picardSubgroup`, `HyperbolicThreeSpace.covolume_picardSubgroup_lt_top`, `HyperbolicThreeSpace.not_compactSpace_quotientGroup_picardSubgroup`. Note: Round AL (AL2\_picard\_group), with the lead's follow-up (Isom⁺(ℋ₃) = PSL(2, ℂ)); reviewed (review/AL2\_picard\_group.md). The tracker v59 gap ('PSL(2, ℤ\[i\]) as a subgroup of PSL(2, ℂ) acting on ℋ₃ by isometries, discrete, of finite covolume and not cocompact') is closed, so every claim of the knowl is proved for the formalisation's objects, under either reading of 'the group of isometries PSL(2, ℂ)' (see (7)). (1) Subgroup: picardToPSL : PSL(2, ℤ\[i\]) →\* PSL(2, ℂ) is Tau Ceti's TauCeti.SpecialLinear.projectiveMap 2 GaussianInt.toComplex (the review replaced the author's pslMap and center\_le\_comap\_center, duplicates of Tau Ceti's projectiveMap and map\_center\_le\_comap\_center at the pin, equal to them by rfl). It is injective (picardToPSL\_injective, from the general HyperbolicThreeSpace.projectiveMap\_injective: for an injective ring hom, a matrix whose image is scalar is scalar). The committed SMul of PicardGroup on ℋ₃ factors through it (picardToPSL\_smul), and picardSubgroup is its range. (2) PSL(2, ℂ) is a group of isometries acting by linear fractional transformations. pslToIsom : PSL(2, ℂ) →\* Isom(ℋ₃) maps into Tau Ceti's group of smooth Riemannian isometries (C\^∞ diffeomorphisms preserving the metric tensor) of TauCeti.UpperHalfSpace ℂ, whose metric (‖dx‖² + dy²)/y² is the knowl's ds = \|dz\|/y (TauCeti.UpperHalfSpace.norm\_def). Its value is the LMFDB coordinate formula moebius (pslToIsom\_apply: pslToIsom γ z = γ • z), and it is injective (pslToIsom\_injective: the fixed points of g ≠ ±1 are null, by hyperbolicVolume\_setOf\_smul\_eq\_self). Proof: an upper triangular matrix acts by a Tau Ceti similarity, (0,-1;1,0) acts by (x, y) ↦ (-x̄, y) after Tau Ceti's inversion in the unit sphere, and g = (c⁻¹, a; 0, c)(0,-1;1,0)(1, d/c; 0, 1) when c ≠ 0. Riemannian isometries also preserve the Riemannian distance (Tau Ceti's RiemannianIsometry.riemannianEDist\_eq), so each element of PSL(2, ℂ) is a metric isometry as well. The formula z ↦ (az + b)(cz + d)⁻¹ holds in Mathlib's quaternions ℍ\[ℝ\] with z = x + yj (toQuaternion\_smul, for a representative of determinant 1). (3) Discrete: discreteTopology\_picardSubgroup, for Mathlib's quotient topology of PSL(2, ℂ) = SL(2, ℂ)/\{±1\}, SL(2, ℂ) with the subspace topology of M₂(ℂ). It comes from the general criterion discreteTopology\_of\_finite: only finitely many elements have a representative with entries of absolute value at most C (finite\_setOf\_mem\_picardSubgroup). (4) Cofinite: exists\_isFundamentalDomain\_picardSubgroup gives a measurable fundamental domain (proper discontinuity, countability, null fixed-point sets). Every fundamental domain has finite hyperbolic volume (hyperbolicVolume\_lt\_top\_picardSubgroup), so Mathlib's covolume is finite (covolume\_picardSubgroup\_lt\_top); Mathlib's covolume is 0 when no fundamental domain exists, which is excluded here by the existence theorem (the docstring says so; Tau Ceti's Subgroup.IsCofinite for Fuchsian groups uses the same covolume). The measure is the committed hyperbolicVolume dx₁ dx₂ dy / y³, the volume element of ds² = (dx₁² + dx₂² + dy²)/y², invariant under PSL(2, ℂ). The volume bound comes from reduction theory, proved directly for ℤ\[i\] (exists\_norm\_le\_one\_and\_le\_height): every point is moved by SL(2, ℤ\[i\]) into \{\|x\| ≤ 1, y ≥ 1/2\}, using a point of maximal height in the orbit, a Gaussian-integer translation and S. The brief's suggested transfer from bianchiPSLGroup σ (bianchiGammaZero 1) was not used: no tree identifies ℤ\[i\] with 𝒪\_K for a number field K (Tau Ceti's GaussianRationals.adjoin\_eq\_top gives 𝒪\_K = ℤ\[θ\] only), and the direct proof is short. The SL₂ image for general K is in BianchiGroupKleinian.lean (record mf.bianchi.bianchigroup), so the GL₂-against-SL₂ index never arises. (5) Not cocompact: Γ \\ ℋ₃ is not compact (not\_compactSpace\_quotient\_picardSubgroup), and neither is PSL(2, ℂ)/Γ, so Γ is not a cocompact subgroup of PSL(2, ℂ) in the group sense either (not\_compactSpace\_quotientGroup\_picardSubgroup). These come from the general not\_compactSpace\_quotient\_of\_height (an element sends height y to y, or to at most 1/y) and compactSpace\_quotient\_of\_compactSpace\_quotientGroup. (6) The committed definition IsPicardMaassForm now has a non-vacuous, well-posed L²(Γ \\ ℋ₃) clause. The Picard group itself has a measurable fundamental domain (exists\_isFundamentalDomain\_picardGroup, via isFundamentalDomain\_picardGroup\_iff). Integrability of an invariant function, such as \|f\|², does not depend on the fundamental domain (integrableOn\_iff\_of\_isFundamentalDomain\_picardGroup). These are the two facts the R4 record called 'not proved here'. The review checked that the constant function 1 satisfies IsPicardMaassForm with eigenvalue 0 (scratch AL2\_picard\_group-review/Probe.lean), so the definition is inhabited. Bases: mf.maass.picard.laplacian is formalised (tracker v59). (7) READING, no longer a judgement call: 'a ... subgroup of the group of isometries PSL(2, ℂ), where the isometries are given by linear fractional transformations' is proved under both readings. (i) 'PSL(2, ℂ), a group of isometries of ℋ₃ acting by linear fractional transformations', the brief's reading: pslToIsom is injective, with pslToIsom\_apply and toQuaternion\_smul. (ii) 'PSL(2, ℂ) is the group of orientation-preserving isometries' (follow-up, OrientationPreservingIsometry.lean): an isometry is orientation-preserving (IsOrientationPreserving) when the Jacobian determinant of its differential in the chart ℂ × ℝ = ℝ³ (jacobianDet; the chart of the open subset ℋ₃ is the inclusion and tangentSpaceCastModel is the identity, so this is the Euclidean Jacobian) is positive; its sign is the same at every point (isOrientationPreserving\_iff\_jacobianDet\_pos). isOrientationPreserving\_iff\_mem\_range shows, for every element of Tau Ceti's Isom (all four cases of Tau Ceti's classification exists\_eq\_similarity\_or\_exists\_eq\_inversion\_mul\_similarity with Mathlib's linear\_isometry\_complex), that these are exactly the elements of the image of pslToIsom, so pslEquivOrientationPreservingIsom : PSL(2, ℂ) ≃\* Isom⁺(ℋ₃) (orientationPreservingIsom, whose carrier is \{Φ \| IsOrientationPreserving Φ\}). Proof: the Jacobian determinants are c³ det A for a similarity (jacobianDet\_similarity) and negative for an inversion (jacobianDet\_inversion\_neg); a similarity with a rotation is the action of an upper triangular matrix (similarity\_rotation\_mem\_range); the inversion in the sphere of radius \|R\| about (a, 0) is the action of (a, \|a\|² − R²; 1, ā)/R after (x, y) ↦ (−x̄, y) (inversion\_eq\_pslToIsom\_mul\_negConjIsom). The literal 'PSL(2, ℂ) is the group of all isometries' is false: (x, y) ↦ (−x̄, y) is an isometry that reverses orientation (not\_isOrientationPreserving\_negConjIsom); this is recorded as an optional fixable wording. pslToIsom stays the underlying map and is no longer in decls. TEXT ERRORS. New, fixable (changes the mathematics), old string once in the live text: '\$ad-bc\\not=0\$' → '\$ad-bc=1\$'. For a matrix of determinant δ, the quaternion (az + b)(cz + d)⁻¹ has j-coefficient yδ/(\|cx + d\|² + \|c\|²y²), which lies in ℋ₃ only for real δ \> 0: diag(i, 1) sends j to k. Optional, fixable (the literal reading is false), once: 'the group of isometries' → 'the group of orientation-preserving isometries' (no overlap with the recorded comma fix). Already recorded in lmfdb-knowl-edits.md, each old string once in the live text: 'z=x+iy' → 'z=x+yj' (in the quaternions) and ' ,where' → ', where'. Verified by the review (scratch AL2\_picard\_group-review/): lake build of the five modules through the guard; \#lint (15 linters, slow ones included) 0 errors on the 160 declarations of the five modules (96 plus 64 generated); \#print axioms on all 160: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound; the decls resolve in their recorded modules; dup\_decls (merge step 3b) 0 clashes; the simp deletion test on 45 lists (124 entries): all needed except conj\_ofReal in toQuaternion\_smul, removed (the shortened list re-tested). Sizes after the review: MoebiusIsometry.lean 239 lines, KleinianGroup.lean 286, PicardGroupKleinian.lean 371, OrientationPreservingIsometry.lean 345 (BianchiGroupKleinian.lean, 217, serves the sibling).
