* [`character.dirichlet.values`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Representations/Dirichlet-characters/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_character___dirichlet___values_FLQQ_--statement) — Values of a Dirichlet character. Declarations (Mathlib · LeanBridge): `DirichletCharacter`, `DirichletCharacter.eq_iff_forall_mem_Icc`, `MulChar.map_one`, `DirichletCharacter.apply_modulus`, `DirichletCharacter.apply_eq_zero_or_exists_rat_apply_eq_exp`, `DirichletCharacter.exists_rat_apply_eq_exp`, `MulChar.map_nonunit`. Note: Round AI (AI2), reviewed. Formalised, with a text correction (fixable text, ruling of 2026-11-11). The knowl is one sentence about a Dirichlet character chi of modulus q \> 1 (Mathlib's DirichletCharacter C q, a MulChar on ZMod q; the LMFDB's function Z -\> C is n -\> chi (n : ZMod q)). (1) 'Complete information ... is contained in the list of values (chi(1), ..., chi(q))': DirichletCharacter.eq\_iff\_forall\_mem\_Icc, chi = psi iff chi n = psi n for every n in \[1, q\] (every residue class has a representative in \[1, q\]), for every q \>= 1, the modulus 1 of the LMFDB included. (2) chi(1) = 1: Mathlib's MulChar.map\_one. (3) chi(q) = 0 for q \> 1: DirichletCharacter.apply\_modulus (false at q = 1, where chi(1) = 1, which is why the knowl takes q \> 1). (4) 'each of which is a root of unity e(r) := exp(2 pi i r), for some rational number r': false as written for the zero values (chi(q) = 0, which the knowl's own list shows, and chi(n) = 0 whenever gcd(n, q) \> 1, Mathlib's MulChar.map\_nonunit). Corrected text, old 'each of which is a root of unity', new 'each of which is either \$0\$ or a root of unity' (the old string occurs once in the live text). Proved: DirichletCharacter.apply\_eq\_zero\_or\_exists\_rat\_apply\_eq\_exp (every value chi a, a : ZMod q, q \>= 1, is 0 or exp(2 pi i r) for some r : Q), from DirichletCharacter.exists\_rat\_apply\_eq\_exp (the value at a unit u is exp(2 pi i r), r = i / \|(Z/qZ)\^x\|, from Mathlib's MulChar.apply\_mem\_rootsOfUnity and Complex.mem\_rootsOfUnity). The LMFDB's table itself shows the values at -1 and at the first integers prime to q only (lmfdb/characters/web\_character.py, Gelts), all roots of unity; the storage and display are a convention. Also a pure typo, recorded: '\$e(r) := \\exp(\{2 \\pi i r\}\$)' closes the math mode before ')'. Review: statements and proofs checked, the modulus q = 1 included (scratch Probe.lean); no statement changed (the variable q hoisted to the file level). lake build through the guard; \#lint (15 linters) clean; axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound; the six public names are new in Mathlib, Tau Ceti and LeanBridge (dup\_decls: 0 clashes).
* [`character.dirichlet.values_on_gens`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Representations/Dirichlet-characters/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_character___dirichlet___values_on_gens_FLQQ_--statement) — Values of a Dirichlet character on generators. Declarations (Mathlib · LeanBridge): `DirichletCharacter`, `DirichletCharacter.eq_iff_forall_apply_eq_of_closure_eq_top`, `DirichletCharacter.exists_rat_apply_eq_exp`, `ZMod.val_mem_Icc_of_isUnit`, `ZMod.natCast_zmod_val`, `MulChar.apply_mem_rootsOfUnity`. Note: Round AI (AI2), reviewed. Formalised. (1) 'A Dirichlet character of modulus q is determined (via multiplicativity) by the values chi(g\_1), ..., chi(g\_r) it takes on any list of generators g\_1, ..., g\_r for the group (Z/qZ)\^x': DirichletCharacter.eq\_iff\_forall\_apply\_eq\_of\_closure\_eq\_top, for any family g : iota -\> (ZMod q)\^x with Subgroup.closure (Set.range g) = top, chi = psi iff chi (g i) = psi (g i) for every i (through Mathlib's MonoidHom.eq\_of\_eqOn\_dense on the unit homomorphisms and MulChar.ext); any modulus q, any index type (iota = Fin r for a list). (2) 'the values chi(g\_i) are roots of unity e(r) := exp(2 pi i r), where r is a rational number': DirichletCharacter.exists\_rat\_apply\_eq\_exp (the value at any unit is exp(2 pi i r) for some r : Q; every q \>= 1). (3) 'The generators g\_i can each be specified as integers in the interval \[1, q-1\]': every unit is the class of an integer in \[1, q - 1\] when q \> 1: ZMod.val\_mem\_Icc\_of\_isUnit (the least nonnegative representative a.val of a unit a lies in \[1, q - 1\]) with Mathlib's ZMod.natCast\_zmod\_val ((a.val : ZMod q) = a). The range q \> 1 is implicit, as it is explicit in character.dirichlet.values: at q = 1 the interval \[1, 0\] is empty. In the LMFDB's setting this never arises: the page shows values on generators only for q \> 2 (lmfdb/characters/templates/Character.html), the generators being Sage's unit generators of Z/qZ (lmfdb/characters/TinyConrey.py), an empty list for q = 1 and q = 2. No text error. Review: statements and proofs checked (scratch Probe.lean: q = 1 with the empty family, q = 3); no statement changed. Checks as for character.dirichlet.values (same file).
