lus 1, S\_a(1 - 1) = 0 but tau\_a = 1, gaussSum\_mulShift\_modOne); the LMFDB has the character 1.1 and its code puts the dot at tau\_0 = 1. Correction (fixable, ruling of 2026-11-11; the old string occurs exactly once in the live text): old 'A large dot marks the last of them, the complete Gauss sum \$\\tau\_a(\\chi) = S\_a(N-1)\$.' new 'A large dot marks the complete Gauss sum \$\\tau\_a(\\chi) = S\_a(N)\$, which for \$N \> 1\$ is the last of them, \$S\_a(N-1)\$.' (b) 'chi(n) = 0 whenever gcd(n, N) \> 1, so each omitted stage would simply repeat the segment before it': partialGaussSum\_succ\_of\_not\_coprime (with Mathlib's MulChar.map\_nonunit). (c) 'If chi is primitive, then \|tau\_a(chi)\| = sqrt N for every a coprime to N, and tau\_a(chi) = 0 for every other a': norm\_gaussSum\_mulShift\_of\_isPrimitive and gaussSum\_mulShift\_eq\_zero\_of\_isPrimitive (from Mathlib's gaussSum\_mulShift\_of\_isPrimitive and star\_gaussSum\_eq and Tau Ceti's gaussSum\_mul\_gaussSum\_inv\_eq\_card\_of\_isPrimitive); 'phi(N) dots on the circle together with a cluster of dots at the origin': ncard\_setOf\_norm\_gaussSum\_mulShift\_eq\_sqrt\_of\_isPrimitive (exactly phi(N) of the tau\_a have absolute value sqrt N, those with a a unit: norm\_gaussSum\_mulShift\_eq\_sqrt\_iff\_of\_isPrimitive, setOf\_norm\_gaussSum\_mulShift\_eq\_sqrt\_of\_isPrimitive). (d) 'a character is primitive exactly when its coprime dots reach the circle': isPrimitive\_iff\_forall\_norm\_gaussSum\_mulShift\_eq\_sqrt, with the stronger norm\_gaussSum\_mulShift\_lt\_sqrt\_of\_not\_isPrimitive (an imprimitive chi has \|tau\_a\| \< sqrt N at every unit a); proof by Parseval, sum\_a \|tau\_a\|\^2 = N phi(N) (sum\_norm\_sq\_gaussSum\_mulShift), and a nonzero Gauss sum at the non-unit N/d, d the conductor (tau\_\{N/d\}(chi) is a positive multiple of tau(psi) for the primitive psi inducing chi). (e) 'Since tau\_a(chi) = conj(chi(a)) tau\_1(chi) for primitive chi and a coprime to N, the dots on the circle are the vert