ntial good reduction (hasPotentialEverywhereGoodReduction\_x\_cube\_sub\_x). Nothing unproved. This also closes ec.reduction (partial on this gap in round ZY): with the global notion, 'has potential good reduction if its j-invariant is integral' is hasPotentialEverywhereGoodReduction\_iff\_isInteger\_j, and the final claim 'if E has potential good reduction then it cannot be semistable unless it has everywhere good reduction' is the new WeierstrassCurve.IsSemistable.hasEverywhereGoodReduction (same file). Review (2026-11-08): confirmed; at every prime of L either 2 or 3 is a unit of the local ring, so the one extension serves all primes, and the equivalence and the example show the predicate is neither vacuous nor trivial. The claim for ec.reduction is confirmed against its text (declarations to link in the review notes).
