n\_iff\_not\_dvd\_LFunction\_apply). The rest of the knowl was formalised before: good/bad reduction (Mathlib's HasGoodReduction, IsBadReduction), the unique singular point (Tau Ceti's Affine.eq\_of\_isSingular\_of\_isSingular), the double point and the nodal/cuspidal/split/non-split definitions (round ZY's NodeCusp: evalEval\_line\_of\_isSingular, evalEval\_vertical\_of\_isSingular, hasMultiplicativeReduction\_iff\_hasNode, hasAdditiveReduction\_iff\_hasCusp, hasSplitMultiplicativeReduction\_iff\_hasSplitNode, isNonsplitMultiplicativeReduction\_iff\_hasNonsplitNode), ordinary = non-trivial p-torsion over F̄\_p (Tau Ceti's IsOrdinary, HasGoodOrdinaryReduction). Nothing unproved. New text error, a pure typo: old 'to obtain a curves over \$\\mathbb F\_p\$', new 'to obtain a curve over \$\\mathbb F\_p\$'; by the ruling of 2026-11-07 it leaves the knowl formalised. Review (2026-11-08): confirmed. The statement is about Mathlib's own L-function (it typechecks against @WeierstrassCurve.LFunction ℚ Rat.instField Rat.numberField W) and covers every prime p (exists\_absNorm\_eq); the two ℚ-algebra structures on ℚ\_v are equal (Algebra ℚ \_ is a subsingleton), so congr! with Subsingleton.elim proves an equality of instance terms and changes no statement. The typo's old text occurs once in knowls\_live.json, the new text nowhere.
