* [`modcurve.xs4.remarks`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___xs4___remarks_FLQQ_--statement) — Remarks on \$X\_\{S\_4\}(\\ell)\$. Declarations (LeanBridge): `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.IsAdelicS4`, `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.IsS4Preimage`, `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.adelicDet`, `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.IsAdelicS4.neg_one_mem_and_map_adelicDet_eq_top_iff`, `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.IsAdelicS4.neg_one_mem`, `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.IsAdelicS4.map_adelicDet_eq_top_iff`, `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.IsS4Preimage.map_det_eq_top_iff`, `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.isS4Preimage_top_three`. Note: Round AI (AI6\_local\_modcurve), from the audit of 2026-11-13 (N2: 'Partially in LeanBridge', medium). Reviewed (review/AI6\_local\_modcurve.md): formalised, confirmed. The knowl, included (KNOWL\_INC) on the family page of X\_\{S4\}(l) below modcurve.xs4: 'The subgroup H contains -I and has surjective determinant when l = +-3 mod 8, but not otherwise.' H is the group of X\_\{S4\}(l) in GL2(Z-hat) of modcurve.xs4 (IsAdelicS4: the inverse image, under reduction modulo l, of the inverse image in GL2(F\_l) of a subgroup of PGL2(F\_l) isomorphic to S4; any such subgroup, so no choice up to conjugacy is needed); surjective determinant is H.map adelicDet = top, as in LeanBridge's modular-curve files (PSL2Index, Agreeable, MinimalTwist). Proved for the adelic H, for every prime l and every such H: IsAdelicS4.neg\_one\_mem (-I in H, always: from the committed IsS4Preimage.neg\_one\_mem and adelicReductionZMod\_neg), IsAdelicS4.map\_adelicDet\_eq\_top\_iff (det(H) = Z-hat\^x iff l % 8 = 3 or 5) and, added by the review, the knowl's sentence itself, IsAdelicS4.neg\_one\_mem\_and\_map\_adelicDet\_eq\_top\_iff (-I in H and det(H) = Z-hat\^x, iff l % 8 = 3 or 5); the same for the level-l group, IsS4Preimage.map\_det\_eq\_top\_iff. Route: the quadratic character of the determinant, chi o det, is trivial on the scalars and factors through PGL2(F\_l); an element g whose image in PGL2(F) has order 4 has tr(g)\^2 = 2 det(g) (sq\_trace\_eq\_two\_mul\_det\_of\_orderOf\_eq\_four, any field F: Cayley-Hamilton g\^2 = t g - d is not scalar so t != 0, and g\^4 = (t\^3 - 2td) g + d\^2 - t\^2 d is scalar while g is not), so chi(det g) = chi(2) (quadraticChar\_det\_eq\_of\_orderOf\_eq\_four); S4 is generated by its elements of order 4 (Equiv.Perm.closure\_orderOf\_eq\_four: (0 1) = (0123)\^2 (0312) and Mathlib's closure\_cycle\_adjacent\_swap); chi(2) = 1 iff l = +-1 mod 8 (Mathlib's ZMod.exists\_sq\_eq\_two\_iff). If l = +-1 mod 8, chi o det is trivial on S, so det(H\_l) lies in the squares and misses a nonsquare; if l = +-3 mod 8, a lift of an element of order 4 (the image of finRotate 4) has nonsquare determinant, and with the scalars (determinants: the squares) det(H\_l) = F\_l\^x. From level l to GL2(Z-hat): map\_adelicDet\_adelicPreimage\_eq\_top\_iff (for every N != 0 and every K \<= GL2(Z/N): det(adelicPreimage N K) = Z-hat\^x iff det(K) = (Z/N)\^x), through the density of SL2(Z) in SL2(Z-hat) (committed exists\_adelicReduction\_sl2zToAdelic\_eq) and Tau Ceti's exists\_mem\_Gamma\_map\_intCast\_zmod\_eq (SL2(Z) onto SL2(Z/N)). l = 2 and 3: at l = 2 no such H exists (24 does not divide \|PGL2(F\_2)\| = 6: the statements are vacuous there, and the knowl's l is odd); at l = 3, PGL2(F\_3) = S4 (isS4Preimage\_top\_three: faithful action on the four points of P\^1(F\_3), Matrix.ProjGenLinGroup.toPermHom\_injective, and \|PGL2(F\_3)\| = 24), so H = GL2(Z-hat), which contains -I and has surjective determinant, as 3 = 3 mod 8 (scratch NonVacuity.lean). Non-vacuity is shown at l = 3 only: the existence of S4 in PGL2(F\_l) for every odd l, with modcurve.xs4's 'unique up to conjugacy', is modcurve.xs4's own gap and not this knowl's claim (for l = +-1 mod 8 the 'not otherwise' half is a statement about every such H, none being exhibited). No text error; a wording suggestion for the editors in the review. Check