* [`shimcurve.discb`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Shimura-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_shimcurve___discb_FLQQ_--statement) — Discriminant of a quaternion algebra. Declarations (LeanBridge): `QuaternionAlgebra.IsRamifiedAt`, `QuaternionAlgebra.IsSplitAt`, `QuaternionAlgebra.discriminant`, `QuaternionAlgebra.finite_setOf_isRamifiedAt`, `QuaternionAlgebra.discriminant_eq_prod`. Note: Ramified (every nonzero element of ℚ\_p ⊗ B a unit) and split were formalised; the gap, finiteness of the ramified set, is now proved: finite\_setOf\_isRamifiedAt shows that a quaternion algebra over ℚ (central simple, dimension 4) is ramified at finitely many primes, and discriminant\_eq\_prod that disc(B), the committed finprod, is the finite product of the ramified primes, as the knowl says. Proof: B ≅ ℍ\[ℚ,a,b\] for some a, b ∈ ℚˣ (LeanBridge's exists\_nonempty\_algEquiv\_of\_finrank\_eq\_four), ℚ\_p ⊗ B ≅ ℍ\[ℚ\_p,a,b\] (Tau Ceti's baseChangeTwoParams), which is ≅ M₂(ℚ\_p) by Tau Ceti's splitting criterion when the norm equation b = x² - a y² is solvable in ℚ\_p, that is, when the Hilbert symbol (a, b)\_p is 1 (not\_isRamifiedAt\_of\_exists\_eq\_sq\_sub\_mul\_sq); and (a, b)\_p = 1 at all but finitely many p by Tau Ceti's hasFiniteMulSupport\_hilbertSymbol\_unitAtFinitePlace, read over ℚ\_p through hilbertSymbol\_unitAtFinitePlace\_rat (both at the pin). Review (ZZ7): the author's own route re-proved that finiteness by Hensel's lemma (exists\_units\_padicInt\_eq, exists\_eq\_sq\_sub\_mul\_sq\_of\_not\_dvd, the primes dividing 2·num(a)·den(a)·num(b)·den(b)) and added the instance HenselianLocalRing ℤ\_\[p\], which the pins already give through Tau Ceti's generic IsAdicComplete.henselianLocalRing and Mathlib's IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal ℤ\_\[p\]) ℤ\_\[p\] (\#synth finds it); both were removed and finite\_setOf\_isRamifiedAt rewritten on the pin's lemmas, which needed a rebuild of 12 stale Tau Ceti modules under TauCeti.NumberTheory.QuadraticForm.Global.HilbertS