* [`shimcurve.level`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Shimura-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_shimcurve___level_FLQQ_--statement) — Level of a Shimura curve. Declarations (LeanBridge): `Subalgebra.enhancedGroupLevel`, `Subalgebra.enhancedGroupKernel`, `Subalgebra.enhancedGroupTopology`, `Subalgebra.exists_enhancedGroupKernel_le_of_isOpen`, `Subalgebra.enhancedGroupLevel_pos_of_isOpen`, `Subalgebra.isLeast_enhancedGroupLevel`, `Subalgebra.enhancedGroupKernel_le_of_level_pos`, `PolarizedQuaternionOrder.isCompact_of_isOpen`. Note: Round AJ (AJ3). The blockers were the profinite topology of the enhanced group, the fact that an open subgroup contains the kernel of reduction modulo some N, and the Shimura curves X\_H. New (same files as shimcurve.index): with the topology Subalgebra.enhancedGroupTopology (product of the profinite topology of O-hat\^x and the discrete topology of Aut\_\{+-mu\}(O)), every open subgroup H of the enhanced group contains ker(O-hat\^x -\> (O/NO)\^x) for some positive integer N (exists\_enhancedGroupKernel\_le\_of\_isOpen: a basic open neighbourhood of 1 in the inverse limit constrains finitely many components N\_1, ..., N\_k, and the kernel modulo N\_1 ... N\_k lies in it), so the committed enhancedGroupLevel (the sInf of the N \> 0 with that kernel in H, 0 if none) is positive for open H (enhancedGroupLevel\_pos\_of\_isOpen), H contains the kernel of reduction modulo it (committed enhancedGroupKernel\_le\_of\_level\_pos) and it is the least positive integer with this property (isLeast\_enhancedGroupLevel). For a polarized order of a quaternion algebra over Q the open subgroups are exactly the open compact subgroups of the knowl (PolarizedQuaternionOrder.isCompact\_of\_isOpen, from the finiteness of Aut\_\{+-mu\}(O), AutPmMuFinite.lean). Second paragraph, 'The level of a Shimura curve X\_H is the level of the corresponding open compact subgroup H': a definition on H, the modcurve.level case (formalised on the group H, X\_H not being formalised), with no theorem about the curve. Proposed formalised. Every sentence is captured; no text error. Review (AJ3): confirmed. isLeast\_enhancedGroupLevel states the knowl's 'least positive integer N such that H contains ker(O-hat\^x -\> (O/NO)\^x)' (least in the usual order, as written) for every open H, with exists\_enhancedGroupKernel\_le\_of\_isOpen supplying the N the definition presupposes. Review edits: enhancedGroupLevel\_pos\_of\_isOpen is now derived from isLeast\_enhancedGroupLevel (the two proofs repeated the same Nat.sInf\_mem term), and the unused lemma enhancedGroupLevel\_le was removed; no linked statement changed.
* [`shimcurve.nrdmu`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Shimura-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_shimcurve___nrdmu_FLQQ_--statement) — Polarization degree of a polarized order. Declarations (LeanBridge): `PolarizedQuaternionOrder.polarizationDegree`, `Rat.squarefreePart`, `PolarizedQuaternionOrder.isSquare_div_polarizationDegree`, `PolarizedQuaternionOrder.eq_polarizationDegree_of_isSquare`, `PolarizedQuaternionOrder.squarefree_polarizationDegree`, `PolarizedQuaternionOrder.reducedNorm_pos`, `PolarizedQuaternionOrder.polarizationDegree_eq_degree`, `QuaternionAlgebra.reducedNorm`. Note: Round AF. Formalised on the ruling of 2026-11-11 (a fixable definition is not partial), with the recorded text error ('the integer nrd(mu)/discrd(O)' need not be an integer: B = (-1,3/Q), O = Z\<1,i,j,ij\>, discrd 12, mu = i, lmfdb-knowl-edits-2026-11-07.md) corrected to 'the square-free part of the positive rational number nrd(mu)/discrd(O)'. New: Nat.squarefreePart n = prod\_p p\^(v\_p(n) mod 2) (squarefree, n = sqf(n) m\^2 with explicit m), Rat.squarefreePart q = sqf(\|num q\| den q), and for q /= 0 it is the unique squarefree natural d with \|q\|/d a rational square (Rat.isSquare\_abs\_div\_squarefreePart, Rat.eq\_squarefreePart\_of\_isSquare, via Nat.eq\_of\_squarefree\_of\_mul\_sq\_eq: padicValRat parity). polarizationDegree = squarefree part of nrd(mu)/discrd(O); reducedNorm\_pos: nrd(mu) = (trd(mu)\^2 - trd(mu\^2))/2 \>= -mu\^2 \> 0 (trd of the integer mu\^2 = m is 2m when dim B = 4), so with discrd(O) \> 0 (shimcurve.disco, quaternionDiscrd\_pos) the quotient is a positive rational; isSquare\_div\_polarizationDegree and eq\_polarizationDegree\_of\_isSquare: deg(mu) is the unique squarefree d with nrd(mu)/(discrd(O) d) a rational square (B a quaternion algebra: central simple of dimension 4). polarizationDegree\_eq\_degree: when the quotient is an integer, as the LMFDB says, deg(mu) is that integer's squarefree part, the committed PolarizedQuaternionOrder.degree (which takes the numerator's squarefree part and is wrong for non-integral quotients, e.g. 1 instead of 3 for 1/12; it should no longer be the main link). The other recorded fix, the squarefree part of the integer nrd(mu) discrd(O), has the same square class and so is the same number. The sweep's second blocker (the reduced discriminant of shimcurve.disco) is gone: shimcurve.disco is formalised. Round AM: PolarizedQuaternionOrder.negOneThree (PolarizedOrderExample.lean) is a concrete polarized order realising the recorded counterexample: discrd(O) = 12, nrd(mu) = 1, polarizationDegree\_negOneThree = 3 against degree\_negOneThree = 1; its polarization 6i has the integral quotient 3, for which polarizationDegree\_eq\_degree applies (review AM2 scratch). No new text error. Review (AF4): formalised, confirmed. Checked in a scratch file: 1/12 has numerator 1 and denominator 12, so the committed degree is the square-free part of 1, that is 1, while Rat.squarefreePart (1/12) is the square-free part of 12, that is 3. The new definition agrees with both fixes recorded on 2026-11-07 wherever they apply: the square-free part of the integer nrd(mu) discrd(O) lies in the same square class, and under a condition on mu making discrd(O) divide nrd(mu) the quotient is an integer and polarizationDegree\_eq\_degree applies. Review change: reducedTrace\_intCast moved from the PolarizedQuaternionOrder namespace to QuaternionAlgebra, the namespace of reducedTrace. Merge: the committed shimuraCurveLabel (Label.lean, LMFDB shimcurve.label, partial) takes its entry delta from PolarizedQuaternionOrder.degree, which is wrong when the quotient is not an integer; it should use polarizationDegree. Lead record of round AM (2026-11-17): note only, outcome and links as AF4.
* [`shimcurve.polarized_order`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Shimura-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_shimcurve___polarized_order_FLQQ_--statement) — Polarized quaternion order. Declarations (LeanBridge): `PolarizedQuaternionOrder`, `Subalgebra.IsPolarization`, `QuaternionAlgebra.IsDivision`, `QuaternionAlgebra.IsIndefinite`, `QuaternionAlgebra.isIndefinite_iff_nonempty_algEquiv_matrix`, `PolarizedQuaternionOrder.nonempty_algEquiv_matrix`, `PolarizedQuaternionOrder.negOneThree`. Note: Round AM (AM2\_quaternion\_orders): outcome unchanged (formalised, round ZY1: the split-or-division dichotomy makes the structure's IsIndefinite B, 'R tensor B is not a division algebra', the indefiniteness of shimcurve.quaternion\_algebra, R tensor B = M2(R), for every quaternion algebra over Q; nothing unproved); the note changes. New: a concrete polarized order, so that PolarizedQuaternionOrder and its corollaries (round AJ's and earlier ones) are not vacuous in Lean (round AJ's review, care point 3 and fold item 6). PolarizedQuaternionOrder.negOneThree (PolarizedOrderExample.lean, 207 lines after the review): B = H\[Q,-1,3\] = (-1, 3 / Q); B is a division algebra (QuaternionAlgebra.isDivision\_negOne\_three: by Tau Ceti's split-or-division dichotomy forall\_isUnit\_or\_nonempty\_algEquiv\_matrix and splitting criterion nonempty\_algEquiv\_matrix\_iff\_exists\_eq\_sq\_sub\_mul\_sq, B is a division algebra unless 3 = x\^2 + y\^2 over Q, which Rat.sq\_add\_sq\_ne\_three refutes: (x, y, 1) would be a nonzero zero of the form x\^2 + y\^2 - 3z\^2, anisotropic over Q by Tau Ceti's TauCeti.NumberField.QuadraticForm.anisotropic\_sumTwoSquaresSubThreeSq at the pin, through the Hilbert symbol (-1, 3) = -1 at 3); B is indefinite (QuaternionAlgebra.isIndefinite\_of\_pos: for b \> 0, R tensor (a, b / Q) = H\[R,a,b\] by Tau Ceti's baseChangeTwoParams, where the nonzero sqrt(b) + j and sqrt(b) - j have product b - j\^2 = 0); B is central simple of dimension 4 (Tau Ceti's instances for H\[K,a,b\], recorded as instances for H\[Q,-1,3\]); the order O = Z + Zi + Zj + Zij is the range of the liftHom of the Z-basis QuaternionAlgebra.Basis.negOneThree (isQuaternionOrder\_negOneThree, through the general QuaternionAlgebra.Basis.isQuaternionOrder\_range\_liftHom of MaximalOrderConjugate.lean); the polarization is mu = i, a unit (inverse -i) with mu\^2 = -1, and trd(mu x) is an integer for x in O because mu x lies in O and the reduced trace is integral on an order (committed exists\_reducedTrace\_eq\_intCast). Checked in scratch (NonVacuity.lean, compiles): the committed corollaries apply to it with finrank\_eq\_four: nonempty\_algEquiv\_matrix (R tensor B = M2(R)), finite\_autPmMu, compactSpace\_enhancedGroup, isCompact\_of\_isOpen and finiteIndex\_of\_isOpen for the open subgroup H = enhancedGroupKernel mu 5, enhancedGroupLevel\_pos\_of\_isOpen, reducedNorm\_pos, isSquare\_div\_polarizationDegree, shimuraCurveLabel. Also proved for this polarized order: discrd(O) = 12 (QuaternionAlgebra.Basis.quaternionDiscrd\_negOneThree: in the Z-basis 1, i, j, ij the reduced trace form is diag(2, -2, 6, 6), via the committed toMatrix\_traceForm\_basisOneIJK), nrd(mu) = 1, PolarizedQuaternionOrder.polarizationDegree\_negOneThree (deg(mu) = 3) and degree\_negOneThree (the committed degree is 1): the counterexample of the recorded shimcurve.nrdmu text error ('the integer nrd(mu)/discrd(O)', here 1/12) and of the docstrings of PolarizationDegree.lean and PolarizedQuaternionOrder.degree, which stated these values without proof. The decl PolarizedQuaternionOrder.negOneThree is an example of the knowl's notion, not a statement of the knowl; it is linked as lattice.extreme links its hexagonal example. No new axioms, no sorry; lake build, \#lint clean, \#print axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. Review (AM2): formalised confirmed. negOneThree meets the committed structure exactly (isDivision, isIndefinite, the order, the unit i with inverse -i, i\^2 = (-1 : Z), trd(i x) integral for x in O), and B is a quaternion algebra over Q through the two recorded instances and finrank\_eq\_four, so every committed corollary applies (the author's NonVacuity.lean, rerun after the review); the one corollary with an extra hypothesis, polarizationDegree\_eq\_degree (nrd(mu)/discrd(O) an integer), cannot apply to mu = i (1/12) but applies to the polarization mu = 6i of the same order (36/12 = 3; review scratch NonVacuity2.lean). Review changes, no statement changed: Rat.sq\_add\_sq\_ne\_three re-proved a special case of the pin's anisotropic\_sumTwoSquaresSubThreeSq from Mathlib's Nat.eq\_sq\_add\_sq\_iff and now follows from it in two lines (the import Mathlib.NumberTheory.SumTwoSquares is replaced by TauCeti.NumberTheory.QuadraticForm.Global.TernaryObstruction, which adds 6 built Tau Ceti modules to the closure); a local have's type moved whole to its continuation line; Nat.prime\_three.squarefree for Irreducible.squarefree Nat.prime\_three; the named arguments (K := Q) replaced by (-1 : Q\^x); the module docstring no longer says that the knowl shimcurve.nrdmu contains the example. Knock-on: shimcurve.nrdmu (formalised, AF4) keeps its outcome and links; its note's sentence 'No concrete PolarizedQuaternionOrder exists in LeanBridge (...)' is now stale (merge instruction in review AM2).
